E["item:empty-leaden-collection-phial"] = {t="item",n="Empty Leaden Collection Phial",z="gnomeregan",s="Ozzie Togglevolt gathers Gnomeregan’s radioactive fallout in a leaden phial. He hopes the residue may help cure his afflicted kin, or make an extraordinarily potent drink.",h="Ozzie Togglevolt gathers Gnomeregan’s radioactive fallout in a leaden phial.",sec={{t="A Shielded Vessel",b="Ozzie Togglevolt made a leaden phial to gather the radiation left in Gnomeregan. The city’s vents once flooded its tunnels with toxic radiation to purge the trogg menace. The surviving defenders became leper gnomes, and the invading beasts were irradiated.\n\nGreen light still clings to Irradiated Invaders and Pillagers prowling the ruins. The lead shields the handler as the phial draws in the dangerous residue. Once sealed, the collection becomes a Full Leaden Collection Phial for Ozzie’s experiments.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the phial used for?",a="The phial gathers radioactive fallout from Irradiated Invaders and Irradiated Pillagers near Gnomeregan’s surface tunnels. Sealed inside, the collection becomes a Full Leaden Collection Phial for research.",al={"what does phial do","how to use empty leaden collection phial","phial purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the phial made of lead?",a="The lead shields the handler from Gnomeregan’s lethal radioactive fallout. Without protection, living beings can suffer severe radiation sickness, and gnomes can become lepers.",al={"why lead phial","why leaden"}},{q="Who created this collection device?",a="Ozzie Togglevolt, a gnome tinkerer, made the phial. He works from Kharanos in Dun Morogh and gives it to those willing to brave Gnomeregan’s toxic outskirts.",al={"who made the phial","ozzie togglevolt phial","who gave me this phial"},it="origin"},{q="What does Ozzie hope to achieve with the collected fallout?",a="Ozzie and his associate Razzle hope the collected fallout will help them invent a cure for leper gnomes afflicted by the catastrophe. Ozzie also allows that their formula might become potent rum or a cure for baldness.",al={"why collect fallout","gnogaine purpose","what is ozzie making"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the Empty Leaden Collection Phial?",a="It is a heavy, shielded container designed specifically to harvest and safely store radioactive fallout from the contaminated creatures roaming the ruins of Gnomeregan. Constructed out of thick lead to protect its bearer from the dangerous emerald glow, the phial allows gnomish researchers to sample the toxic residue without succumbing to the sickness that warped the fallen city.",al={"what is empty leaden collection phial","leaden collection phial","empty phial gnomeregan"},it="identity",add="8d10cd55"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For exiled gnomes, Gnomeregan’s ruin remains an open wound. Any attempt to reverse its toxic fallout carries personal stakes, however eccentric the researcher.",["profession:Engineering"]="The leaden phial pairs heavy metal shielding with suction apparatus to collect volatile environmental particles safely. It is a practical piece of gnomish engineering."},kw={"empty leaden collection phial","fallout","gnogaine","gnomeregan","kharanos","leaden phial","ozzie togglevolt","radiation"},rel={"quest:2926","item:full-leaden-collection-phial","npc:ozzie-togglevolt","zone:gnomeregan","topic:leper-gnome","topic:trogg","subzone:kharanos","quest:2962"},src={"Empty Leaden Collection Phial","Gnogaine"}}
E["item:essential-artificial"] = {t="item",n="Essential Artificial",z="gnomeregan",s="In Ironforge, Essential Artificial parts help gnomish tinkers and engineers rebuild after exile. The gnomes left stockpiles behind when they fled Gnomeregan.",h="In Ironforge, Essential Artificial parts help gnomish tinkers and engineers rebuild after exile.",sec={{t="Standard Issue Ingenuity",b="Before Gnomeregan fell, tinkers relied on the Essential Artificial as a component for many uses. Gnomish engineers fitted it into contraptions, clockwork wonders and heavy machinery throughout the subterranean halls. Its standard design let smiths and machinists exchange parts with confidence.",sp=0},{t="Salvage from the Depths",b="The trogg invasion and radiation disaster drove the gnomes from Gnomeregan in a desperate rush. Large stores of Essential Artificial parts remained in heavy, steam-powered dispensers called artificial extrapolators, scattered through the deeper passages.\n\nIn Tinker Town, master craftsman Klockmort Spannerspan seeks daring adventurers to return to the contaminated ruins and recover the parts. He needs them so research and invention can continue.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an Essential Artificial?",a="The Essential Artificial is a standardized mechanical component. Gnomish smiths and tinkers use it in experiments, machines and contraptions.",al={"what are essential artificials","essential artificial item","what is this component"},it="identity"},{q="Why were they left behind in Gnomeregan?",a="The trogg invasion and deadly radiation forced the gnomes to flee in a rush. Stockpiles of everyday components remained in storage devices.",al={"why are they in gnomeregan","why abandoned"}},{q="Who wants these components recovered?",a="Klockmort Spannerspan, an ambitious inventor in Tinker Town within Ironforge, seeks the parts for his experiments and technological research in exile.",al={"who needs essential artificials","who takes these","klockmort spannerspan quest"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are they found inside the ruins?",a="Large, steam-powered containers called artificial extrapolators hold Essential Artificial parts throughout the deeper levels of contaminated Gnomeregan.",al={"where do i find essential artificials","artificial extrapolator location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where do essential artificials come from, and who made them?",a="Essential artificials are precision mechanical components engineered and manufactured by the tinkers and smiths of Gnomeregan before the fall of their great city. Produced in bulk for gnomish technology, they were stored inside automated dispensers known as artificial extrapolators placed in the city's deeper industrial complexes.",al={"who made essential artificials","essential artificial origin","where do essential artificials come from"},it="origin",add="691fb1fc"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, recovering components from Gnomeregan's irradiated corridors helps your people rebuild their technological superiority while taking refuge in Ironforge.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how these widely used parts fit varied machinery and experimental designs."},kw={"artificial extrapolator","engineering component","essential artificial","gnomeregan","klockmort spannerspan","tinker town"},rel={"quest:2924","quest:2925","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge"},src={"Essential Artificial","Essential Artificials"}}
E["item:full-leaden-collection-phial"] = {t="item",n="Full Leaden Collection Phial",z="gnomeregan",s="In Kharanos, Ozzie Togglevolt seeks a sample from Gnomeregan’s troggs. He hopes it will cure irradiated leper gnomes, or perhaps make a dangerously potent rum.",h="In Kharanos, Ozzie Togglevolt seeks a sample from Gnomeregan’s troggs.",sec={{t="A Toxic Brew",b="A lead lining shields the bearer from the volatile green fallout saturating Gnomeregan. High Tinker Mekkatorque’s advisors flooded the lower corridors with toxic radiation to stop the invading troggs. Instead, the disaster corrupted troggs and surviving gnomes into maddened, irradiated horrors.\n\nIrradiated Invaders and Pillagers leave fluid residue for refugee tinkerers in Kharanos. Ozzie Togglevolt and Razzle Sprysprocket use it as raw material in their experiments on remedies.",sp=0},{t="Cure or Concoction",b="Ozzie Togglevolt experiments frantically to address the fallout, while Gnoarn remains fixed on reclaiming the city. Ozzie hopes the liquid will treat an entrapped leper gnome and perhaps reverse his own baldness. In gnome laboratories, the line between a miraculous antidote and a highly volatile beverage remains dangerously thin.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is the phial made of lead?",a="The phial’s lead lining shields its bearer from intense radioactive fallout gathered from Gnomeregan’s contaminated troggs. That lets them carry it back to Kharanos without sickness or death.",al={"why leaden phial","why lead flask","leaden collection phial purpose"},it="item"},{q="Who wants this irradiated fluid?",a="Ozzie Togglevolt, a gnome researcher in Kharanos, wants the irradiated fallout to experiment on a cure for leprosy-afflicted gnomes. Razzle Sprysprocket helps him.",al={"who needs the phial","ozzie togglevolt quest","who turns in gnogaine"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where does the radiation in the phial come from?",a="The glowing green residue comes from Irradiated Invaders and Irradiated Pillagers, troggs prowling the tainted corridors leading into Gnomeregan.",al={"how to fill phial","irradiated troggs location","green glow source"},it="origin"},{q="Does Ozzie actually cure the leper gnomes with it?",a="Ozzie’s experiments are chaotic and uncertain. His concoction aims to cure a captured leper gnome and restore his own hair, but gnome science often needs repeated testing and refined samples to find safe, consistent results.",al={"does the cure work","gnogaine outcome","is leper gnome cured"}},{q="What is the Full Leaden Collection Phial?",a="It is a heavy, lead-shielded flask filled with glowing green radioactive fallout harvested directly from the contaminated troggs infesting Gnomeregan. The thick lead casing prevents the hazardous radioactive residue from poisoning whoever carries it.",al={"what is leaden phial","full leaden phial","what is this phial"},it="identity",add="32cc4509"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For exiled gnomes in Dun Morogh, carrying this toxic sample recalls the disaster that poisoned their ancestral home. It offers desperate hope of restoring their corrupted kin.",["profession:Engineering"]="The lead casing reflects gnome safety protocols for handling volatile, toxic fallout in laboratory testing."},kw={"full leaden collection phial","gnogaine","gnomeregan","irradiated trogg","kharanos","leaden collection phial","leper gnome","ozzie togglevolt"},rel={"quest:2926","item:empty-leaden-collection-phial","npc:ozzie-togglevolt","zone:gnomeregan","quest:2962","subzone:kharanos","topic:leper-gnome","npc:gnoarn"},src={"Full Leaden Collection Phial","Gnogaine"}}
E["item:heavy-leaden-collection-phial"] = {t="item",n="Heavy Leaden Collection Phial",z="gnomeregan",s="In Kharanos, Ozzie Togglevolt offers the Heavy Leaden Collection Phial for decontamination research. It is meant to draw in unstable irradiated discharge from mutants deep inside Gnomeregan and keep it contained.",h="In Kharanos, Ozzie Togglevolt offers the Heavy Leaden Collection Phial for decontamination research.",sec={{t="A Shielded Vessel",b="The Heavy Leaden Collection Phial draws volatile residue from living, irradiated creatures in Gnomeregan. Keeping the fallout inside is difficult. A suitable sample may take several attempts to collect.",sp=0},{t="Pursuit of a Cure",b="Ozzie Togglevolt provides the phial to help his research into reversing the terrible mutations afflicting leper gnomes. Earlier samples from surface troggs were too weak for useful chemical analysis.\n\nWith the leaden phial, researchers hope to gather samples from virulent beasts, including irradiated slimes and lurkers in the Hall of Gears. They seek the active elements in the city's toxic fallout, then hope to make an effective antidote.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Heavy Leaden Collection Phial used for?",a="The phial siphons concentrated radioactive discharge from living, irradiated creatures inside Gnomeregan. Researchers in Kharanos use the samples in decontamination trials.",al={"what does this phial do","phial purpose","what is leaden phial"},it="purpose"},{q="Who provides the Heavy Leaden Collection Phial?",a="Ozzie Togglevolt, a gnome researcher in Kharanos in Dun Morogh, provides the phial for his research into curing irradiated and afflicted leper gnomes.",al={"who gives phial","where do i get phial","phial questgiver"},it="origin"},{q="Why is the phial made of heavy lead?",a="The phial is described as heavy and leaden, but its precise construction is not explained. Ozzie warns that containing the radioactive fallout is difficult and the sample will collapse quickly.",al={"why lead phial","why heavy lead"},it="identity"},{q="Which creatures must be sampled with the phial?",a="The phial must be used on living, glowing horrors deep inside Gnomeregan. These include irradiated slimes, lurkers, and horrors prowling the lower levels of the Hall of Gears.",al={"what do i use it on","target creatures","which monsters glow"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Why does Ozzie Togglevolt want the Heavy Leaden Collection Phial returned?",a="Ozzie Togglevolt needs both the phial and a sample of high-potency radioactive fallout returned to his workshop in Kharanos. Having previously tested weaker trogg specimens and deemed them insufficient, he requires pristine, uncorrupted radiation straight from the creatures inside Gnomeregan to advance his experiments in curing the afflicted leper gnomes.",al={"why return heavy leaden phial","why does ozzie want the phial","why is the collection phial needed"},it="why_wanted",add="ca9f55e0"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, every bit of volatile fallout secured in the phial brings you closer to reclaiming Gnomeregan and understanding the chemical madness that stole your home.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can use the phial to collect volatile fallout. Even with a suitable vessel, collecting a sample may take several attempts."},kw={"gnomeregan","hall of gears","heavy leaden collection phial","ozzie togglevolt","phial","radioactive fallout","the only cure is more green glow"},rel={"item:high-potency-radioactive-fallout","quest:2962","quest:2926","subzone:hall-of-gears","subzone:kharanos","zone:gnomeregan","topic:leper-gnome","topic:gnome"},src={"Heavy Leaden Collection Phial","The Only Cure is More Green Glow"}}
E["item:high-potency-radioactive-fallout"] = {t="item",n="High Potency Radioactive Fallout",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan's depths, researchers seek potent radioactive fallout. They hope to learn how the sludge afflicted the leper gnomes and find a cure.",h="In Gnomeregan's depths, researchers seek potent radioactive fallout.",sec={{t="Straight from the Tap",b="Deep in the Hall of Gears, irradiated horrors, lurkers, and slimes roam Gnomeregan's lowest tiers. Researchers outside the fallen capital need fallout drawn from these living creatures. Samples scraped from contaminated scavengers outside are too weak for their work.\n\nThe sludge decays quickly. It must be sealed in a leaden phial and reach the researchers before its potency fades.",sp=0},{t="A Search for Restoration",b="Ozzie Togglevolt and his colleagues seek a cure for the leper gnomes. They believe the secrets of the irradiated sludge may show them the way. During the trogg invasion, toxic venting deformed these survivors and drove them mad.\n\nThe leper gnomes remain trapped in a living nightmare. For the researchers, dangerous expeditions into the ruins are worth the risk.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this radioactive fallout come from?",a="The fallout comes from living irradiated creatures deep in the lower tiers of Gnomeregan's Hall of Gears, including slimes, horrors, and lurkers.",al={"where to get fallout","fallout location","source of radioactive fallout"},it="origin"},{q="Why is this sample needed?",a="Gnomish researchers, including Ozzie Togglevolt, need a concentrated sample of Gnomeregan's radiation to study the affliction and seek a cure for the leper gnomes.",al={"who wants the fallout","fallout purpose","why collect fallout"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why must it be handled so carefully?",a="The fallout decays quickly and loses its potency. It must be carried in a leaden phial and returned to the researchers before it degrades.",al={"fallout decay","why lead phial","fallout unstable"},it="danger"},{q="Why wasn't earlier trogg residue good enough?",a="Residue from troggs outside the city was too weak and impure for testing. Researchers need raw, concentrated fallout from creatures deep within irradiated Gnomeregan.",al={"why not trogg glow","trogg radiation vs fallout","previous sample failure"},it="motive"},{q="What is High Potency Radioactive Fallout?",a="This fallout is a concentrated, volatile residue harvested directly from the deeply irradiated slimes, horrors, and lurkers churning within the ruined halls of Gnomeregan. Highly unstable and glowing with virulent toxic energy, it represents the raw contaminant lingering at the very heart of the disaster.",al={"what is high potency radioactive fallout","radioactive fallout lore","what is the fallout"},it="identity",add="30a827ed"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Each sample of toxic fallout from Gnomeregan's depths offers a frail hope of reversing the mutation that tore your kin apart during the city's fall.",["profession:Engineering"]="Volatile fallout decays quickly, so carry it in purpose-built leaden phials to shield yourself from exposure."},kw={"gnomeregan","green glow","hall of gears","high potency radioactive fallout","irradiated slime","leper gnome","ozzie togglevolt"},rel={"quest:2962","item:heavy-leaden-collection-phial","quest:2926","zone:gnomeregan","subzone:hall-of-gears","topic:leper-gnome","subzone:clean-zone","quest:2927"},src={"High Potency Radioactive Fallout","The Only Cure is More Green Glow"}}
E["item:prismatic-punch-card"] = {t="item",n="Prismatic Punch Card",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, the Prismatic Punch Card bears the highest security clearance. Gnome refugees in Ironforge seek the records it unlocks.",h="In Gnomeregan, the Prismatic Punch Card bears the highest security clearance.",sec={{t="A Matter of Security",b="When the gnomes fled Gnomeregan, troggs and toxic irradiation drove them from the city. Vast stores of research and civic records remained in its depths. The gnomes guarded high-level systems behind tiers of clearance. To reach the Matrix Punchograph 3005-D in the lower Engineering Labs, a card must pass through a series of terminals.\n\nThe card begins white, then advances through yellow, blue, and red. At the final terminal, it is stamped Prismatic. Its encoded clearance is listed as awaiting the invention of an entirely new number.",sp=0},{t="The Vital Transmission",b="Master Mechanic Castpipe sends adventurers from Ironforge's refugee enclaves into Gnomeregan's contaminated halls to recover data he calls vital and impossible to live without. The binary message on the Prismatic Punch Card reveals the transmission's contents: Castpipe is being told his laundry is ready for pickup.",sp=1}},faq={{q="How do you create a Prismatic Punch Card?",a="Insert a Red Punch Card into the Matrix Punchograph 3005-D in Gnomeregan's lower Engineering Labs. First, upgrade a White Punch Card in sequence through the A, B, and C model terminals across the complex.",al={"how to get prismatic punch card","make prismatic punch card","punch card upgrade sequence"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="What data is stored on the Prismatic Punch Card?",a="The card gives its security rating as awaiting the invention of a new number, then carries a long string of binary code. Master Mechanic Castpipe says the data is vital.",al={"what does the card say","punch card binary translation","decoded punch card"},sp=1},{q="Who wants the Prismatic Punch Card?",a="Master Mechanic Castpipe, an exiled gnome engineer in Ironforge, requests the card during Data Rescue. He says it holds urgent, invaluable information left behind when the gnomes evacuated Gnomeregan.",al={"who turns in prismatic punch card","castpipe quest","who needs the card"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are the Matrix Punchograph terminals located?",a="The terminals are spread across Gnomeregan by clearance tier. Punchograph 3005-A is near the surface Train Depot and Workshop entrance. Model B is in the Dormitory beyond the Clean Zone, model C lies deeper in the complex, and model D is in the lower Engineering Labs.",al={"terminal locations","where are the punchographs","where to punch cards"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is a Prismatic Punch Card?",a="A Prismatic Punch Card is an extraordinarily high-clearance data card generated by the computational systems within Gnomeregan. Its automated security classification is supposedly so elevated that gnomish mathematics has yet to invent an adequate number to describe it. In truth, it holds encoded binary text produced by deep-city terminals, functioning as the apex of the gnomes' tiered data-retrieval protocol.",al={"what is prismatic punch card","prismatic punch card lore","prismatic card gnomeregan"},it="identity",add="f4168582"},{q="Where does the Prismatic Punch Card come from, and who made it?",a="The card is produced deep within the fallen city of Gnomeregan by the Matrix Punchograph 3005-D, a high-security automated terminal found on the lower level of the Engineering Labs. It is not handcrafted by a person, but rather encoded by the gnomes' mechanized network when a user feeds a properly upgraded Red Punch Card into the apparatus.",al={"prismatic punch card origin","who made prismatic punch card","where to get prismatic punch card"},it="origin",add="7551673e"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see the Punchograph security system as gnomish ingenuity and bureaucracy still at work after the fall of your home.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see sequential punch-card programming and an automated terminal network as examples of the high standard of computing machinery built by Gnomeregan's tinkerers."},kw={"castpipe","data rescue","engineering labs","gnomeregan","matrix punchograph","prismatic punch card"},rel={"quest:2930","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","subzone:engineering-labs","subzone:train-depot","subzone:dormitory","subzone:clean-zone","topic:gnome"},src={"Prismatic Punch Card","Data Rescue"}}
E["item:robo-mechanical-guts"] = {t="item",n="Robo-Mechanical Guts",z="gnomeregan",s="In Stormwind, Shoni gathers parts from Gnomeregan’s roaming machines. She needs them to repair tunneling vehicles built to help reclaim the city in Dun Morogh.",h="In Stormwind, Shoni gathers parts from Gnomeregan’s roaming machines.",sec={{t="Salvage for the Fleet",b="After High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and the surviving gnomes fled Gnomeregan, thousands of machines remained behind. Automated mechanisms, clockwork sentries, and industrial robots still roam the radioactive city’s corridors.\n\nIn Stormwind City, tinker Shoni is assembling gyrodrillmatic excavationators to break through Gnomeregan’s defenses and reclaim the lost city. She sends adventurers into the contaminated halls to salvage working parts from the robots, including springs, wires, and gyro-components.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Robo-Mechanical Guts used for?",a="Shoni in Stormwind City gathers Robo-Mechanical Guts to repair gyrodrillmatic excavationators. These tunneling vehicles are meant to help reclaim Gnomeregan in Dun Morogh.",al={"what are robot guts for","robo-mechanical guts use","why collect mechanical guts"},it="why_wanted",gp=true},{q="Where do you find these components?",a="You can salvage these components from hostile clockwork automatons, mechs, and contaminated hostiles roaming Gnomeregan’s outskirts and depths.",al={"where to get robo mechanical guts","robot guts drop location","gnomeregan robot parts"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Who is Shoni and why does she need so many parts?",a="Shoni is a gnome engineer stationed in Stormwind’s Dwarven District. She needs parts to prepare nearly four hundred subterranean excavation machines to breach Gnomeregan’s occupied ruins.",al={"who is shoni","shoni stormwind","gyrodrillmatic excavationator fleet"},it="people"},{q="What are Robo-Mechanical Guts?",a="They are the tangled internal machinery, gears, wiring, and salvageable mechanical components stripped from the clockwork automatons wandering Gnomeregan. Though little more than scrap to the untrained eye, these functional guts provide crucial raw mechanisms that ingenious gnome engineers can repurpose for complex vehicular projects.",al={"what are robo-mechanical guts","robo mechanical guts item","what are robo guts"},it="identity",add="b1d0efc3"},{q="Where do Robo-Mechanical Guts come from, and who made them?",a="These assemblies originated within the workshops of Gnomeregan, crafted by gnomish inventors to power their automated workforce and city defenses. When the irradiated disaster struck and High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered the evacuation, countless mechanical constructs were abandoned inside, where they continue roaming the ruined passages with their inner workings still intact.",al={"who made robo-mechanical guts","where do robo mechanical guts come from","robo mechanical guts origin"},it="origin",add="cf2ae288"},{q="Why does anyone want Robo-Mechanical Guts?",a="Shoni the Shilent in Stormwind desperately requires them as replacement components to repair an entire fleet of gyrodrillmatic excavationators. With limited supplies in the human capital, she looks to the rogue mechs in Gnomeregan as an abundant salvage yard to keep her engineering fleet operational.",al={"why collect robo-mechanical guts","who wants robo mechanical guts","why does shoni want robo mechanical guts"},it="why_wanted",add="f52d09f9"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Each tangle of wiring and gyro-cog comes from gnomish automated designs. Radiation and isolation changed the machines, and now they roam.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, salvaging the rogue clockwork sentries of your lost home can feel bittersweet. Their machinery provides parts to help reclaim Gnomeregan."},kw={"clockwork","dun morogh","gnomeregan","gyrodrillmatic excavationators","robo-mechanical guts","shoni","stormwind"},rel={"quest:2928","zone:gnomeregan","zone:dunmorogh","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},src={"Robo-Mechanical Guts","Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators"}}
E["item:techbot-s-memory-core"] = {t="item",n="Techbot's Memory Core",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, Tinkmaster Overspark seeks Techbot's Memory Core to study the automaton's corrupted behavior.",h="In Gnomeregan, Tinkmaster Overspark seeks Techbot's Memory Core to study the automaton's corrupted behavior.",sec={{t="A Polarized Brain",b="Before Gnomeregan fell, Techbot aided Tinkmaster Overspark and his fellow inventors with devices and knowledge. During the city's fall, an errant electrical discharge jolted Techbot and turned its positronic brain to a hostile negatronic state. Now the automaton wanders Gnomeregan's tainted halls and attacks anyone in sight. Overspark hopes the memory core will help him understand the fault and restore his creation to its senses.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Techbot's Memory Core?",a="Techbot's Memory Core holds Techbot's data and knowledge. Techbot is the automaton built by Tinkmaster Overspark, and its core records the electrical disruption that corrupted it during Gnomeregan's fall.",al={"techbots memory core","techbot brain item","what is techbots core"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants Techbot's Memory Core?",a="Tinkmaster Overspark wants Techbot's Memory Core. He has taken refuge with fellow exiled gnomes in Ironforge's Tinker Town. He asks adventurers to enter Gnomeregan, disable Techbot and bring back the core so he can attempt repairs.",al={"who needs techbot memory core","who turns in techbot core","where do i take techbots core"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why did Techbot go berserk?",a="During Gnomeregan's fall, a stray electrical spark jolted Techbot's positronic brain. The surge polarized it into a negatronic state, turning its personality and protocols from helpful to violently frenzied.",al={"why is techbot hostile","what happened to techbot","techbot gone crazy"}},{q="Where is the core obtained?",a="The core is recovered from Techbot, which roams Gnomeregan's upper mechanical corridors and entrances in Dun Morogh.",al={"where to get techbot memory core","techbot location","how to get techbots brain"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Where does Techbot's Memory Core come from, and who made it?",a="The memory core comes from Techbot, a complex mechanical construct built by Tinkmaster Overspark in Gnomeregan. Overspark designed the machine to assist him and his fellow inventors with an endless store of data and gizmos. However, when Gnomeregan fell to the troggs, a rogue electrical surge jolted Techbot and polarized its positronic brain into a negatronic state, driving the machine wild.",al={"who made techbot memory core","techbot origin","who built techbot"},it="origin",add="a503508b"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes, Techbot is another casualty of Gnomeregan's fall. The city's ruin claimed brilliant peacetime engineering.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see how a single electrical short polarized Techbot's positronic brain and inverted its logic."},kw={"brain","gnomeregan","memory core","negatronic","overspark","positronic","techbot","tinker town"},rel={"quest:2922","quest:2923","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","zone:dunmorogh"},src={"Techbot's Memory Core","Save Techbot's Brain!"}}
E["npc:dark-iron-ambassador"] = {t="npc",n="Dark Iron Ambassador",z="gnomeregan",s="Deep in Gnomeregan, the Dark Iron Ambassador moves among the ruined halls as an envoy of his clan. Why the clan has come to the fallen gnome capital remains unclear.",h="Deep in Gnomeregan, the Dark Iron Ambassador moves among the ruined halls as an envoy of his clan.",sec={{t="A Shadowy Envoy",b="In Gnomeregan’s irradiated halls, the Dark Iron Ambassador speaks for his clan. The purpose of his mission is unknown.",sp=0},{t="Conspiracies in the Deep",b="Investigators and goblins suspect the Dark Irons have a hand in Gnomeregan’s troubles and its mysterious super rig. For now, those suspicions remain theories. The ambassador’s presence does not prove who caused the city’s fall or what terms, if any, were agreed upon.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is the Dark Iron Ambassador?",a="The Dark Iron Ambassador is an emissary of his clan inside Gnomeregan. His precise diplomatic mission is unknown.",al={"who is this dwarf","dark iron ambassador identity","what is dark iron ambassador"},it="identity"},{q="Why is a Dark Iron dwarf inside Gnomeregan?",a="His purpose is unclear. His presence shows the Dark Iron clan has an interest in Gnomeregan.",al={"why are dark irons in gnomeregan","what is he doing here","dark iron dwarf purpose"},it="why_here"},{q="Did the Dark Irons help cause the fall of Gnomeregan?",a="No one knows. Investigators suspect the Dark Irons, but their theories do not prove who caused the disaster.",al={"did dark irons cause trogg invasion","dark iron conspiracy","did thaurissan help thermaplugg"},it="conflict"},{q="Where does the ambassador come from?",a="He belongs to the Dark Iron clan, ruled by Emperor Dagran Thaurissan.",al={"where is ambassador from","who sent him","who does he work for"},it="origin"},{q="Is he allied with Mekgineer Thermaplugg?",a="An alliance is suspected, but his presence alone confirms no agreement.",al={"thermaplugg dark iron ally","is he with thermaplugg","working with thermaplugg"},it="allies"},{q="Where can the Dark Iron Ambassador be found?",a="The Dark Iron Ambassador is an elusive, rare encounter in Gnomeregan’s contaminated engineering sectors and workshop corridors.",al={"ambassador spawn location","where does he spawn","ambassador gnomeregan location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is the Dark Iron Ambassador on?",a="He is affiliated with the Dark Iron clan.",al={"dark iron ambassador faction","who does the ambassador serve","dark iron ambassador allegiances"},it="side",add="694fcc25"},{q="What does the Dark Iron Ambassador want?",a="His precise mission and objectives in Gnomeregan are unknown.",al={"dark iron ambassador goal","why did dark irons come to gnomeregan","dark iron ambassador motive"},it="wants",add="e7a948f2"},{q="Who is the Dark Iron Ambassador tied to?",a="He represents the Dark Iron clan. A connection with Mekgineer Thermaplugg has been suspected, but the nature of that connection is unconfirmed.",al={"dark iron ambassador connections","who does the ambassador answer to","dark iron ambassador emperor"},it="ties",add="388c8a07"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you may find the Dark Iron emissary in Gnomeregan troubling. His presence raises questions for gnome investigators.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you may see the Dark Iron dwarf in the ruined gnome city draw attention from Ironforge allies.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you have reason to examine the Dark Iron presence in Gnomeregan."},kw={"conspiracy","dark iron ambassador","dark iron clan","gnomeregan","super rig","thaurissan","thermaplugg"},rel={"npc:sicco-thermaplugg","zone:gnomeregan","topic:dark-iron-clan","topic:dark-iron-dwarf","quest:2947","quest:2904","zone:ironforge"},src={"Dark Iron Ambassador"}}
E["npc:electrocutioner-6000"] = {t="npc",n="Electrocutioner 6000",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan's Launch Bay, Electrocutioner 6000 guards the upper platform. The spider tank fights for Mekgineer Thermaplugg and the irradiated leper gnomes who follow him.",h="In Gnomeregan's Launch Bay, Electrocutioner 6000 guards the upper platform.",sec={{t="Thermaplugg's Shocking Machine",b="After Gnomeregan fell, Mekgineer Thermaplugg and the irradiated leper gnomes who follow him took control of the city's war machines. Electrocutioner 6000 guards the Launch Bay's upper platform. It strikes intruders with high-voltage current.",sp=0},{t="The Workshop Key",b="Electrocutioner 6000 guards the Workshop Key, which opens Gnomeregan's back door into its workshops. Bring down the machine, and the key gives you a quicker route into the city's depths.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can the Electrocutioner 6000 be found?",a="Electrocutioner 6000 stands on an elevated catwalk platform overlooking Gnomeregan's Launch Bay.",al={"electrocutioner 6000 location","where is electrocutioner","find electrocutioner 6000"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who pilots the Electrocutioner 6000?",a="No pilot is named in the accounts of Gnomeregan's fall. Electrocutioner 6000 fights for Mekgineer Thermaplugg and the leper gnomes who follow him.",al={"who drives electrocutioner 6000","pilot of electrocutioner"},it="identity"},{q="Why is the machine so volatile?",a="Its armored chassis channels high-voltage current and unleashes it on anyone who comes near. That makes Electrocutioner 6000 a dangerous guardian of the Launch Bay.",al={"why does it shock","electrocutioner prototype","thermaplugg design"},it="power"},{q="Why is defeating the Electrocutioner 6000 important for explorers?",a="Electrocutioner 6000 guards the Workshop Key, which opens Gnomeregan's back door into its deeper engineering sectors. The key gives you a faster route through the facilities.",al={"workshop key","why kill electrocutioner","electrocutioner 6000 loot"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Is the Electrocutioner an automaton or a vehicle?",a="Electrocutioner 6000 is a mechano-tank, an armored, spider-legged war machine of gnomish make. It now fights those seeking to free Gnomeregan.",al={"is electrocutioner a robot","electrocutioner spider tank type"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Electrocutioner 6000?",a="The Electrocutioner 6000 is a super-charged mechanical spider tank guarding the Launch Bay in Gnomeregan. Crackling with high-voltage current, it fights for Mekgineer Thermaplugg and the leper gnomes who follow him.",al={"who is electrocutioner 6000","what is electrocutioner 6000","electrocutioner 6000 lore"},it="identity",add="cad4dd7a"},{q="Whose side is the Electrocutioner 6000 on?",a="The war machine fights entirely in service of Mekgineer Thermaplugg and his faction of crazed leper gnomes. It zealously defends Thermaplugg's claim over Gnomeregan, annihilating any troggs, Alliance operatives, or Horde interlopers who venture near the Launch Bay.",al={"electrocutioner faction","who does electrocutioner serve","electrocutioner allegiance"},it="side",add="48c81a6d"},{q="What does the Electrocutioner 6000 want?",a="The tank serves the megalomania of Mekgineer Thermaplugg. Its purpose is to electrocute and eradicate any trespassers who dare enter Gnomeregan's deeper sectors.",al={"electrocutioner 6000 goal","what does electrocutioner want","electrocutioner motive"},it="wants",add="5513927c"},{q="Why is the Electrocutioner 6000 in the Launch Bay?",a="Stationed high upon the upper catwalks of the Launch Bay, the tank guards the elevated walkways and locks down access deeper into the complex. It carries the Workshop Key, serving as a heavily armed checkpoint against anyone attempting to penetrate the heart of Thermaplugg's stronghold.",al={"why is electrocutioner here","why is electrocutioner in launch bay","electrocutioner purpose"},it="why_here",add="e5de5943"},{q="Why is the Electrocutioner 6000 feared?",a="The machine is notorious for its lethal output. Its armored chassis channels high-voltage current that it unleashes on anyone who comes near, making it one of the most dangerous guardians between intruders and the heart of Thermaplugg's stronghold.",al={"why is electrocutioner feared","electrocutioner reputation","why is electrocutioner famous"},it="fame",add="06482735"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As an exiled gnome of Ironforge, you may see Electrocutioner 6000 as an insult to your craft: a gnomish war machine turned against its own people under Thermaplugg's rule.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can marvel at the high-voltage output harnessed within Electrocutioner 6000's chassis, even as it is turned against you.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an ally, you know breaching the Launch Bay and destroying Electrocutioner 6000 is vital to securing the Workshop Key. It lets you bypass hazardous front corridors while seeking to free Gnomeregan."},kw={"electrocutioner","gnomeregan","launch bay","spider tank","thermaplugg","workshop key"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:launch-bay","topic:leper-gnome","topic:gnome","zone:ironforge"},src={"Electrocutioner 6000"}}
E["npc:kernobee"] = {t="npc",n="Kernobee",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, Kernobee lies trapped among the ruins. The goblin engineer found Dark Iron dwarves working on the great super rig, then was captured, beaten unconscious, and left among the troggs in the dormitory quarters.",h="In Gnomeregan, Kernobee lies trapped among the ruins.",sec={{t="A Deadly Discovery",b="While doing business or scavenging in Gnomeregan, Kernobee learned that Dark Iron dwarves had helped build and operate the great super rig burrowing beneath the city. He knew the danger of that discovery and tried to flee to Ratchet. There he meant to warn his associate, Tinkerwiz. The Dark Irons caught him before he could escape.",sp=0},{t="Left for the Troggs",b="Kernobee's captors beat him unconscious and left him alive. They threw him into a small room along the dormitory corridor, opposite the Clean Zone. Feral troggs and radiation surround him. He needs help to wake, reach safety, and escape the ruins.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Kernobee?",a="Kernobee is a goblin operative found unconscious in Gnomeregan's dormitory sector. He works closely with Tinkerwiz in Ratchet and entered the ruins before his attackers caught him.",al={"who is this goblin","kernobee lore","about kernobee"},it="identity"},{q="Why was Kernobee imprisoned in Gnomeregan?",a="Kernobee discovered that the Dark Iron clan was helping build subterranean super rig machines inside Gnomeregan. The Dark Irons knocked him unconscious and threw him into the dormitory to die, keeping their presence and sabotage quiet.",al={"why is he here","why did dark irons capture him","why in dormitory"},it="why_here"},{q="Who does Kernobee report to?",a="Kernobee reports to Tinkerwiz, a goblin engineer in Ratchet, the neutral port town across the sea in the Barrens.",al={"who is tinkerwiz","where is he going","ratchet connection"},it="ties"},{q="Where in Gnomeregan is Kernobee located?",a="Kernobee lies unconscious in a small side room on the Dormitory's lower level, on its western side directly across from the Clean Zone.",al={"kernobee location","where is kernobee","find kernobee"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Kernobee on?",a="Kernobee is affiliated with the Steamwheedle Cartel, answering to Tinkerwiz in the neutral port of Ratchet. Rather than serving the Alliance or the Horde, he operates on goblin business—which placed him squarely against the Dark Iron dwarves lurking within Gnomeregan once he uncovered their schemes.",al={"is kernobee alliance or horde","kernobee faction","who does kernobee work for"},it="side",add="3c758521"},{q="What does Kernobee want?",a="Kernobee wants nothing more than to escape Gnomeregan alive. After discovering that Dark Iron dwarves were involved in constructing the massive super rig, he urgently needs to make it out of the dormitory and flee the irradiated city so he can report his findings back to Tinkerwiz in Ratchet.",al={"what is kernobee trying to do","kernobee goal","why help kernobee"},it="wants",add="b63dca8d"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes fighting to reclaim their homeland, Kernobee's discovery shows that Dark Iron dwarves aided their catastrophe from the shadows.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know the danger of exploring experimental subterranean machinery like the Dark Iron rigs while rival schematics are at stake."},kw={"dark iron","dormitory","gnomeregan","kernobee","ratchet","super rig","tinkerwiz"},rel={"quest:2904","zone:gnomeregan","subzone:dormitory","subzone:clean-zone","subzone:ratchet","topic:goblin","topic:trogg"},src={"Kernobee"}}
E["npc:nogg"] = {t="npc",n="Nogg",z="gnomeregan",s="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Nogg puts his craft to work for the Horde. He studies strange mechanical salvage from deep within Gnomeregan.",h="In Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor, Nogg puts his craft to work for the Horde.",sec={{t="Nogg's Workshop",b="Nogg keeps an independent engineering workshop in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. Adventurers and craftsmen seek the mechanical skill of a goblin in a city famed for orcish steel and strength. He eagerly examines unusual devices and trinkets brought from Alliance lands or underground ruins.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Gadgets and Salvage",b="Salvage from Gnomeregan draws Nogg's special attention. Horde operatives recover intricate rings and other remnants from the fallen gnomish capital. Few minds in Durotar can take apart those strange clockwork devices, decipher them, and adapt them for Horde use.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Nogg?",a="Nogg works from his engineering workshop in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor.",al={"nogg location","where is nogg","nogg's machine shop"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Nogg's connection to Gnomeregan?",a="Horde adventurers salvage intricate devices from Gnomeregan's irradiated tunnels in Khaz Modan. Nogg inspects and reconfigures the gnomish rings they bring back.",al={"why nogg gnomeregan","nogg ring","return of the ring"},it="ties"},{q="Is Nogg part of the Horde?",a="Nogg is an independent goblin artisan in Orgrimmar who serves Horde adventurers with his technical skill.",al={"is nogg horde","nogg faction"},it="side"},{q="Can Nogg alter or reforge rings?",a="Yes. Bring Nogg a Sparklematic-extracted ring from Gnomeregan, and he can dismantle and rebuild it with different enchantments or mechanical properties.",al={"ring redo","change gnomeregan ring"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Who is Nogg?",a="Nogg is an enterprising goblin engineer running Nogg's Machine Shop in the Valley of Honor in Orgrimmar. Like many goblins residing in the Horde's capital, he plies his mechanical trade to tinkerers and adventurers alike, maintaining a keen commercial and practical eye for intriguing contraptions and technological salvage.",al={"who is nogg","nogg lore","nogg identity"},it="identity",add="81166680"},{q="What does Nogg want?",a="Nogg wants innovative engineering parts, curious mechanical artifacts, and lucrative opportunities. His interests include examining intricate rings salvaged by adventurers and keeping an eye on the technological chaos of conflicts like the rig wars in Gnomeregan to bolster his shop's business.",al={"what does nogg want","nogg goals","nogg quests purpose"},it="wants",add="c0d235dc"},{q="Why is Nogg in Orgrimmar?",a="Nogg operates out of the Valley of Honor in Orgrimmar, where the bustling capital offers a steady flow of clientele, raw materials, and adventurous mercenaries willing to run dangerous errands. His machine shop thrives on the constant demand for engineering expertise among the Horde.",al={"why is nogg here","why is nogg in orgrimmar","nogg location reason"},it="why_here",add="0ba8fca5"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can visit Nogg's workshop in the Valley of Honor for parts and talk. You can also watch him repurpose intricate gnomish devices with ease.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warrior returning from dangerous operations in the Eastern Kingdoms, you can bring Nogg crude salvage. He can turn it into finely calibrated battle gear."},kw={"gnomeregan","goblin engineer","machine shop","nogg","orgrimmar","return of the ring"},rel={"zone:orgrimmar","quest:2947","quest:2950","zone:gnomeregan","topic:goblin","topic:horde"},src={"Nogg"}}
E["npc:ozzie-togglevolt"] = {t="npc",n="Ozzie Togglevolt",z="gnomeregan",s="In Kharanos, Ozzie Togglevolt works with Razzle Sprysprocket to find a cure for the leper gnomes of Gnomeregan. Their research continues among the snowy hills of Dun Morogh.",h="In Kharanos, Ozzie Togglevolt works with Razzle Sprysprocket to find a cure for the leper gnomes of...",sec={{t="Escape from the Deep",b="Ozzie Togglevolt was deep inside Gnomeregan when catastrophe struck. Toxic fallout filled the corridors to stem the trogg invasion. Ozzie stood beside Gnoarn when a sudden radioactive discharge changed Gnoarn forever. Ozzie escaped to the surface and reached Dun Morogh alive, but the disaster stayed with him.",sp=0},{t="The Kharanos Workshop",b="In Kharanos, Ozzie spends his days tinkering with Razzle Sprysprocket. Their work is personal. They seek a way to reverse the mutagenic fallout from their lost home and cure the suffering leper gnomes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Ozzie Togglevolt?",a="Ozzie Togglevolt is a gnome engineer in Kharanos, Dun Morogh. He escaped the radioactive devastation of Gnomeregan and now uses his skills to seek a cure for his afflicted kin.",al={"who is ozzie","ozzie togglevolt lore","kharanos gnome ozzie"},it="identity"},{q="What is Ozzie trying to cure?",a="Ozzie and Razzle Sprysprocket are researching a way to cleanse the toxic irradiation that turned many of their kin into leper gnomes stricken with madness.",al={"what is ozzie researching","ozzie leper gnome cure","cure for leper gnomes"},it="wants"},{q="Who is Gnoarn to Ozzie?",a="Gnoarn was beside Ozzie in Gnomeregan when the toxic vents were unleashed. Ozzie saw a radioactive bolt strike Gnoarn, driving his determination to reverse the contamination.",al={"ozzie and gnoarn","what happened to gnoarn","who is gnoarn"},it="ties"},{q="Who is working with Ozzie in Kharanos?",a="Ozzie works with Razzle Sprysprocket in Kharanos. Together, they tinker, develop concoctions, and gather contaminated field specimens to study the radioactive fallout.",al={"ozzie partner","who is razzle","razzle sprysprocket"},it="allies"},{q="What quests does Ozzie offer?",a="Ozzie asks travelers in Dun Morogh to gather irradiated residues and components from around Gnomeregan through 'The Day After', 'Gnogaine', and 'The Only Cure is More Green Glow'.",al={"ozzie quests","togglevolt quests","what quests does ozzie give"},gp=true},{q="Whose side is Ozzie Togglevolt on?",a="Ozzie stands squarely with the Gnomeregan Exiles and the Alliance. Like many survivors of Gnomeregan's devastating fall, he has taken refuge among the dwarves in Dun Morogh, dedicating his mind and skills entirely to assisting his fellow displaced gnomes.",al={"ozzie togglevolt faction","ozzie togglevolt alliance or horde","who does ozzie togglevolt serve"},it="side",add="86f7524c"},{q="Why is Ozzie Togglevolt here in Dun Morogh?",a="Ozzie fled to Kharanos following the tragic contamination of Gnomeregan. Having escaped the lethal radiation that corrupted so many of his brethren, he set up shop with fellow tinkerers to establish a safe base close enough to study the fallout and help survivors.",al={"why is ozzie togglevolt in kharanos","why is ozzie here","ozzie togglevolt location reason"},it="why_here",add="3c84fab0"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnome adventurers, Ozzie embodies the grief and resolve of Gnomeregan's survivors. He refuses to abandon his irradiated kin to their fate.",["profession:Engineering"]="For an engineer, Ozzie's work shows the trial and error of gnome craft. Devices can backfire in combat or lead to breakthroughs in biochemical decontamination.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can find Ozzie in Kharanos, just outside Ironforge. He aids travelers while the Alliance holds its foothold in Dun Morogh's frigid hills."},kw={"dun morogh","gnoarn","gnomeregan","kharanos","leper gnome","ozzie","radiation","razzle","sprysprocket","togglevolt"},rel={"npc:razzle-sprysprocket","npc:gnoarn","topic:leper-gnome","subzone:kharanos","zone:gnomeregan","quest:2927","quest:2926","quest:2962"},src={"Ozzie Togglevolt"}}
E["npc:scooty"] = {t="npc",n="Scooty",z="gnomeregan",s="From Booty Bay’s busy pirate port, Scooty keeps a teleport link to Gnomeregan. The goblin engineer trusts his craft and his transponders, though the experimental pad lies in the fallen gnome city. For the Horde, his device opens a perilous route into Dun Morogh.",h="From Booty Bay’s busy pirate port, Scooty keeps a teleport link to Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="Booty Bay's Teleportation Expert",b="Among Booty Bay’s wharves and workshops, Scooty pursues ambitious tinkering for the Steamwheedle Cartel. While many goblins favor gunpowder and explosives, he works to move matter across great distances. His transponders keep a working link to a teleportation pad inside Gnomeregan. Horde forces rely on his craft to reach the subterranean gnome stronghold without crossing dangerous Alliance territory.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Gadgets and Goblin Risk",b="Experimental goblin teleporters rarely run without a hitch. After hearing of a new gnomish rig in Gnomeregan, Scooty and his partner Sovik built the Transpolyporter 6000. Scooty cheerfully admits it has exploded a dozen or so times. Crossing continents as scattered matter carries clear physical dangers, yet Scooty remains sure of his genius. To him, every mechanical failure is a small obstacle on the road to innovation.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Scooty?",a="Scooty works as a goblin engineer in Booty Bay and claims to be a master engineer. He maintains and calibrates the Goblin Transponder network, which links the port to an experimental teleportation pad deep inside Gnomeregan.",al={"who is scooty","scooty lore","scooty npc","booty bay scooty"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Scooty have a teleporter to Gnomeregan?",a="Scooty linked Booty Bay to an experimental teleportation pad inside Gnomeregan to allow direct travel into the gnome city. For the Horde, it offers an indispensable route into Dun Morogh without crossing the heavily fortified Alliance homelands.",al={"why gnomeregan teleporter","how does scooty teleporter work","scooty port to gnomer"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is Scooty located?",a="Scooty works in Booty Bay, the neutral goblin port at the southern tip of Stranglethorn Vale.",al={"where is scooty","scooty location","find scooty"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is using Scooty's teleporter safe?",a="Scooty’s teleporter successfully sends adventurers into Gnomeregan, but its workings can go awry. Mechanical mishaps and miscalibrated transponders make each trip a hazard.",al={"is scooty safe","teleporter safe","teleporter risks"},it="danger"},{q="Whose side is Scooty on?",a="Scooty operates out of Booty Bay as part of the neutral goblin enterprise. He maintains his engineering services and experimental transport device for any traveler willing to do business, regardless of their faction ties.",al={"scooty faction","is scooty horde or alliance","scooty allegiance"},it="side",add="6ce6cf89"},{q="Why is Scooty in Booty Bay?",a="Operating out of Booty Bay gives Scooty access to independent trade networks and curious adventurers far from the meddling oversight of mainland authorities. Here, he can manage his transponder network and tinker with long-range goblin teleportation at his own leisure.",al={"why is scooty here","scooty booty bay why","what brought scooty here"},it="why_here",add="04182db4"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can use Scooty’s indispensable shortcut into Gnomeregan to bypass Alliance defenses in Dun Morogh.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate Scooty’s audacious use of transponder physics, though goblin disregard for safety makes every activation a gamble."},kw={"booty bay","gnomeregan","goblin","scooty","stranglethorn","teleporter","transponder"},rel={"subzone:booty-bay","zone:gnomeregan","quest:2904","topic:goblin"},src={"Scooty"}}
E["npc:sicco-thermaplugg"] = {t="npc",n="Mekgineer Thermaplugg",z="gnomeregan",s="In ruined Gnomeregan, Mekgineer Thermaplugg rules from a massive mechanical battle suit. Once High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque’s trusted advisor, he brought about the city’s irradiation in a bid for power. The fallout made him a leper gnome and left him deranged, ruling the ruined halls.",h="In ruined Gnomeregan, Mekgineer Thermaplugg rules from a massive mechanical battle suit.",sec={{t="A Toxic Ambition",b="For many years, Mekgineer Thermaplugg advised High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque, who trusted him completely. Yet Thermaplugg secretly coveted the High Tinker’s office. Even Mekkatorque cannot say what drove his advisor to betray that trust. He can only wonder whether Thermaplugg sought power or wealth, both of which he would have had in time.",sp=0},{t="The Poisoning of Gnomeregan",b="During the Third War, troggs swarmed Gnomeregan from below, and the gnomes fought them in the dark. Seeking a way to break the siege, Gelbin asked Thermaplugg for counsel. Thermaplugg urged him to flood the city with radioactive gas, claiming it would destroy the troggs and spare the gnomes. He meant instead to use the crisis to unseat Mekkatorque and seize power.",sp=1},{t="King of the Ruins",b="Thermaplugg’s gamble went terribly wrong. Radioactive fallout swept through every level of Gnomeregan, killing eighty percent of its gnomes and twisting many survivors into feral, diseased leper gnomes. The radiation warped Thermaplugg too and drove him utterly mad.\n\nThermaplugg crowned himself King of the Gnomes and rules among irradiated machines and mutated thralls. His forces fight trogg invaders and surface gnomes seeking to reclaim their lost home.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Mekgineer Thermaplugg?",a="Before betraying his people during the trogg invasion, Mekgineer Thermaplugg was High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque’s chief advisor. He urged Mekkatorque to release radioactive gas into Gnomeregan so he could seize power. The gas nearly extinguished the gnomish population, and Thermaplugg now rules the irradiated ruins as a mad king.",al={"who is thermaplugg","thermaplugg lore","who is the boss in gnomeregan","thermaplugg backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Thermaplugg betray Gelbin Mekkatorque?",a="Even Mekkatorque cannot say for certain why Thermaplugg betrayed him. The High Tinker wonders if Thermaplugg sought power or wealth, both of which he would have had in time. Thermaplugg had long coveted the High Tinker’s office and used the trogg crisis to seize Gnomeregan for himself.",al={"why did he betray gnomeregan","thermaplugg motive","why does sicco hate gelbin"},it="motive"},{q="Did Thermaplugg cause the trogg invasion?",a="Troggs first broke into Gnomeregan’s lower levels after they were unearthed from the ancient titan vault of Uldaman. Rumors say Thermaplugg knew of the breach or even helped bring it about to create a crisis. Mekkatorque has never verified whether Thermaplugg started the invasion or simply exploited it.",al={"did he summon troggs","did sicco bring the troggs","trogg invasion gnomeregan origin"},it="threat"},{q="What happened to Thermaplugg after the gas was released?",a="Thermaplugg suffered lethal radiation along with thousands of other gnomes. The fallout withered his flesh, turned his skin sickly green, and fractured his mind. He stayed behind to rule the ruins as the self-proclaimed King of the Gnomes instead of fleeing with surviving refugees to Ironforge.",al={"is thermaplugg a leper gnome","how did he become a leper gnome","why is thermaplugg green"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Crowd Pummeler 9-60?",a="The Crowd Pummeler 9-60 is a hulking gnomish war machine that still stomps through Gnomeregan’s Engineering Labs. It is one of many mechanical guardians defending Thermaplugg’s irradiated domain.",al={"crowd pummeler origin"},it="item"},{q="What does High Tinker Mekkatorque want done with Thermaplugg?",a="Mekkatorque regards Thermaplugg as his greatest failure and his people’s greatest traitor. From his temporary court in Ironforge’s Tinker Town, he commissions brave Alliance adventurers to enter Gnomeregan’s irradiated depths and execute Thermaplugg. He seeks justice for the fallen.",al={"gelbin quest thermaplugg","kill thermaplugg quest","does mekkatorque want him dead"}},{q="Whose side is Mekgineer Thermaplugg on?",a="Thermaplugg serves only himself and his twisted ambition. He betrayed the Alliance and his own people when he flooded Gnomeregan with radioactive gas, driving the survivors into exile. Cut off from the outside world and utterly corrupted by radiation, he now commands the leper gnomes who remain within the ruined city, ruling over them as a mad despot while battling both the invading troggs and any outsiders who dare breach his domain.",al={"thermaplugg faction","who does thermaplugg serve","sicco thermaplugg allegiance"},it="side",add="83ef33e1"},{q="What does Mekgineer Thermaplugg want?",a="Thermaplugg wants to keep the crown he seized. Having declared himself king of the gnomes, he rules the ruined capital from its depths, commanding the leper gnomes and machines that remain, and refuses to give up his rule, though Mekkatorque calls him the king of nothing.",al={"thermaplugg goal","what is thermaplugg planning","sicco thermaplugg motive"},it="wants",add="4bd94cd3"},{q="Why is Mekgineer Thermaplugg here?",a="Thermaplugg remains deep inside Gnomeregan's engineering quarters because he seized the fallen city during the catastrophe. Rather than fleeing to Ironforge with the surviving gnomes, he stayed behind to claim the empty halls and command the mutated leper gnomes who were transformed alongside him. Operating from the Tinkers' Court, he continues to direct his defenses, machines, and twisted followers from the very heart of the disaster that befell the city.",al={"why is thermaplugg in gnomeregan","why did thermaplugg stay","thermaplugg location why"},it="why_here",add="7e175e39"},{q="Why is Mekgineer Thermaplugg famous or feared?",a="Thermaplugg is infamous as the greatest traitor in gnomish history. Once celebrated as High Tinker Mekkatorque's chief advisor, his betrayal led directly to the irradiation of Gnomeregan and the loss of the vast majority of its population. The gnomes regard his betrayal with profound horror, fearing both the lethal machines he commands and the utter madness that now guides his despotic rule.",al={"why is thermaplugg feared","thermaplugg reputation","why do gnomes hate thermaplugg"},it="fame",add="cac8a4d9"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Thermaplugg embodies what your people mourn and despise. His vanity and treachery cost you your homeland and turned your kin into diseased horrors.",["faction:Alliance"]="Thermaplugg’s betrayal kept Gnomeregan from answering the call to arms in the Third War. It crippled Alliance supply lines and engineering support during humanity’s darkest hour.",["profession:Engineering"]="Thermaplugg shows the lethal danger of sloppy formulas and unprincipled design. He wields hazardous walking war machines and toxic bomb Dispensers against anyone who enters his workshop.",["race:Dwarf"]="Your kin in Ironforge gave refuge to survivors fleeing Thermaplugg’s poison. Ironforge guards watch the Dun Morogh gates closely against his irradiated wanderers."},kw={"crowd pummeler","gnomeregan","leper gnome","mekkatorque","sicco","thermaplugg","tinkers court","trogg"},rel={"npc:gelbin-mekkatorque","zone:gnomeregan","topic:leper-gnome","topic:gnome","subzone:tinkers-court","zone:ironforge","topic:trogg","subzone:uldaman"},src={"Sicco Thermaplugg"}}
E["npc:talvash-del-kissel"] = {t="npc",n="Talvash del Kissel",z="gnomeregan",s="In Ironforge's Mystic Ward, the gnome jeweler Talvash del Kissel is down on his luck. He fled Gnomeregan when the troggs overran it, then fell into debt amid rumors of questionable dealings. Now he turns to adventurers to recover lost treasures and restore shattered relics. His eye for gems and ancient baubles makes him a valued contact for those exploring Uldaman.",h="In Ironforge's Mystic Ward, the gnome jeweler Talvash del Kissel is down on his luck.",sec={{t="From Artisan to Exiled Debtor",b="Talvash once earned respect as a jeweler in Gnomeregan, until the troggs overran the city and destroyed his livelihood along with his home. He escaped with the surviving refugees to Ironforge and set up camp in the Mystic Ward. Yet relocation brought little relief.\n\nRumors of questionable dealings and unpaid obligations gathered around him, leaving the craftsman in deep financial distress. Unable to rebuild his trade through conventional means, he now relies on freelance adventurers to recover lost assets and salvage his reputation.",sp=0},{t="Relics of Uldaman and Gnomish Craft",b="Talvash has kept his precision with gems and his skill at judging their worth. When explorers in the Badlands uncover an ancient, shattered necklace deep in Uldaman's Titan vault, few craftsmen in the Eastern Kingdoms can make sense of its intricate enchantments. Restoring its power takes rare components and painstaking work. Talvash is eager to do it, both to clear his debts and prove his skill endures.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Talvash del Kissel?",a="Talvash is a gnome jeweler exiled from Gnomeregan who now lives in Ironforge's Mystic Ward. Burdened by debt and rumors, he hires adventurers to repair artifacts and settle his accounts.",al={"who is talvash","talvash del kissel","talvash"}},{q="Where can I find Talvash?",a="Talvash lives in Ironforge's Mystic Ward, near the pond and the magic-oriented shops.",al={"talvash location","where is talvash","find talvash del kissel"}},{q="What happened to his business in Gnomeregan?",a="Talvash ran a jewelry trade in Gnomeregan before the troggs invaded and the city fell. He lost everything, and rumors and poor fortunes left him deeply indebted in Ironforge.",al={"why is talvash broke","talvash debt","what happened to talvash"}},{q="What is Talvash's connection to Uldaman?",a="Explorers who find a shattered power source in Uldaman's ancient dig site are directed to Talvash. His skill with gems and enchanting lets him reconstruct the shattered necklace for adventurers who gather its missing pieces.",al={"talvash uldaman","uldaman necklace","shattered necklace quest"}},{q="Does Talvash have anything to do with Gnomeregan quests?",a="Yes. Talvash helps recover personal items left behind during Gnomeregan's evacuation, including lost rings and devices.",al={"talvash gnomeregan","return of the ring quest"}}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="Talvash shows how Gnomeregan's fall shattered ordinary civilian lives, leaving master craftsmen as broke exiles scraping by in Ironforge.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance adventurers exploring Uldaman or Gnomeregan's ruins can turn to Talvash to restore ancient jewelry and recover lost gnomish heirlooms."},kw={"del kissel","gnomeregan","ironforge","jeweler","mystic ward","shattered necklace","talvash","uldaman"},rel={"zone:ironforge","subzone:mystic-ward","zone:gnomeregan","subzone:uldaman","quest:2947","quest:2948","quest:8355"},src={"Talvash del Kissel"}}
E["npc:viscous-fallout"] = {t="npc",n="Viscous Fallout",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan's lower passages, Viscous Fallout drifts through the toxic runoff.",h="In Gnomeregan's lower passages, Viscous Fallout drifts through the toxic runoff.",sec={{t="A Polluted Spirit",b="Radiation flooded Gnomeregan after Mekgineer Thermaplugg advised a treacherous plan to wipe out the invading troggs. The fallout filled the city's lower levels with toxic slime and contamination. Viscous Fallout is a water elemental, its substance thick with the city's toxic waste. Its origins before the fall are unknown.",sp=0},{t="Agony in the Runoff",b="Viscous Fallout drifts through Gnomeregan's irradiated lower passages as a living pool of toxic sludge. It spews volleys of toxin, then lashes out at anything in its path. Those who enter the city to cleanse its tainted depths must destroy the creature.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Viscous Fallout?",a="Viscous Fallout is a water elemental mini-boss in Gnomeregan's ruined city, tainted by toxic sludge and radioactive fallout.",al={"who is viscous fallout","viscous fallout lore","what kind of mob is viscous fallout"},it="identity"},{q="How did it become corrupted?",a="Radiation flooded Gnomeregan after Mekgineer Thermaplugg treacherously advised using it to repel the trogg invasion. Toxic waste filled the lower passages. No one knows exactly how the elemental became poisoned; it is part of the irradiated ruin the city has become.",al={"why is it green","why is the elemental toxic","how was viscous fallout created"},it="origin"},{q="Where in Gnomeregan does it wander?",a="Viscous Fallout wanders the lower irradiated passages and runoff canals beneath Gnomeregan's main entry paths. It blends among the mutated slimes and toxic waste that infest the area.",al={"viscous fallout location","where to find viscous fallout","how to find viscous fallout"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is it hostile?",a="Like much of what haunts the irradiated depths, Viscous Fallout lashes out at living creatures that trespass in the tainted passages.",al={"why does it attack","can it be saved"},it="hostile"},{q="Does it have any connection to Ironforge?",a="The connection is indirect. Gnomes who fled Gnomeregan now live as refugees in Tinker Town inside Ironforge, while Viscous Fallout remains among the horrors in the home they lost.",al={"hydrocane ironforge","gnome connection"}},{q="Can the elemental be cleansed or cured?",a="No cure is known for the elemental. Radiation and toxic chemicals have permeated its form so thoroughly that destroying it is the only answer.",al={"can you cure viscous fallout","cleanse viscous fallout"}},{q="Whose side is Viscous Fallout on?",a="Viscous Fallout serves no master and belongs to no faction. While its toxic state is the direct result of Mekgineer Thermaplugg venting radioactive fallout across the city, the creature is not allied with him, the leper gnomes, or the troggs. It is simply a tortured elemental, maddened by pollution and lashing out indiscriminately at anything that crosses its path.",al={"viscous fallout faction","who does viscous fallout serve","is viscous fallout with thermaplugg"},it="side",add="c0463f1a"},{q="What does Viscous Fallout want?",a="The elemental has no grand ambition or rational purpose. A toxic mass of the poison that fouled Gnomeregan, it wanders the irradiated corridors and lashes out at any living creature unfortunate enough to enter the city's flooded passages.",al={"viscous fallout goal","what does viscous fallout do","viscous fallout motive"},it="wants",add="41523791"},{q="Why is Viscous Fallout here?",a="It wanders the irradiated depths of Gnomeregan, which were left awash in toxic waste when Mekgineer Thermaplugg flooded the city with radiation to drive back the troggs. Where the elemental came from before the city's fall is not known.",al={"why is viscous fallout in gnomeregan","how did viscous fallout get here","viscous fallout location reason"},it="why_here",add="2b056577"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomes, Viscous Fallout recalls the damage Mekgineer Thermaplugg inflicted on their home, where even the water runs toxic.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you can recognize a water elemental defiled by artificial toxic waste.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see Viscous Fallout as a living wound upon nature, showing the harm reckless industry brings when contamination seeps into underground waters."},kw={"gnomeregan","hydrocane","radiation","thermaplugg","tinker town","viscous fallout","water elemental"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:tinker-town","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome","topic:druid"},src={"Viscous Fallout"}}
E["quest:2904"] = {t="quest",n="A Fine Mess",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, you find Kernobee battered among the troggs after a Dark Iron ambush. His rescue brings word of a drilling rig beneath Dun Morogh, bound for Booty Bay.",h="In Gnomeregan, you find Kernobee battered among the troggs after a Dark Iron ambush.",sec={{t="A Battered Survivor",b="You find Kernobee in Gnomeregan’s dormitory, beaten and groggy. Dark Iron dwarves ambushed the goblin and left him among the feral troggs. You guide him through the contaminated corridors toward safety.",sp=0},{t="Subterranean Schemes",b="Kernobee carries word of the Dark Iron clan’s work on a massive super rig beneath Dun Morogh. He escapes across the sea to Ratchet to warn the goblin engineer Tinkerwiz. Then he sends you south to Booty Bay with news for the goblin engineer Scooty.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Kernobee?",a="Kernobee is a goblin you find beaten nearly to death in Gnomeregan. Dark Iron dwarves ambushed him and left him among the troggs before his rescue.",al={"kernobee","who is kernobee"},it="identity"},{q="Where must Kernobee be escorted?",a="You guide Kernobee through Gnomeregan’s hostile halls toward the Clockwerk Run exit and the upper entrance corridors.",al={"where do i take kernobee","escort destination","clockwerk run exit"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why were the Dark Iron dwarves involved?",a="The Dark Iron dwarves were helping design and build an enormous super rig drill underground. Kernobee discovered their plot before they ambushed him.",al={"why dark iron","dark iron super rig","dark iron in gnomeregan"},it="threat"},{q="Where does Kernobee go after escaping?",a="After reaching safety, Kernobee travels across the sea to Ratchet in the Barrens to warn Tinkerwiz about the Dark Iron involvement in the subterranean drilling rig.",al={"where did kernobee go","kernobee ratchet","tinkerwiz warning"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why must you report to Scooty in Booty Bay?",a="Scooty is a goblin engineer in Booty Bay who works with Tinkerwiz on high-tech subterranean equipment and transponder networks.",al={"why scooty","booty bay turn in","scooty connection"},it="purpose"},{q="How does this relate to Mekgineer Thermaplugg?",a="Scooty knows of the threat Mekgineer Thermaplugg poses inside Gnomeregan. Helping Kernobee provides aid and supplies to adventurers preparing to return and confront the treacherous Mekgineer.",al={"thermaplugg connection","fight thermaplugg"},it="ties"},{q="Why does Kernobee need to be escorted out?",a="Kernobee was ambushed, beaten nearly to death by Dark Iron dwarves, and discarded in a dormitory overrun with hostile troggs. Battered and trapped deep within the ruined halls of Gnomeregan, he cannot survive the journey to the exit on his own. Crucially, he also carries urgent intelligence: he discovered that the Dark Iron clan is directly involved in constructing a massive drilling rig. Escaping with his life is his only chance to travel to Ratchet and warn his associate Tinkerwiz before that machinery wreaks further havoc.",al={"why help kernobee","kernobee motive","why does kernobee need help"},it="motive",add="73352f2e"},{q="Why can't Kernobee escape Gnomeregan on his own?",a="Kernobee is barely conscious when you discover him, having been severely battered by his Dark Iron captors before they tossed him into a pit of troggs. Bruised, unarmed, and weakened within an inch of his life, he has no hope of fighting past the irradiated mutants, rogue constructs, and feral troggs patrolling the Clockwerk Run without a capable adventurer to shield him.",al={"why does kernobee need you","why can't kernobee fight","why me kernobee"},it="why_me",add="9976ada5"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you have a duty of honor to rescue a survivor from Gnomeregan’s contaminated depths. Dark Iron infiltrators and feral troggs threaten him.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you learn that Emperor Thaurissan’s agents are sabotaging Alliance recovery efforts in Gnomeregan.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you may worry to learn that Dark Iron machinists are building a massive super rig underground."},kw={"booty bay","clockwerk run","dark iron","gnomeregan","kernobee","scooty","super rig","tinkerwiz","troggs"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","npc:kernobee","npc:scooty","subzone:clockwerk-run","subzone:dormitory","subzone:booty-bay","subzone:ratchet"},m={start="Kernobee",["end"]="Scooty",level="30",id=2904},src={"A Fine Mess"}}
E["quest:2922"] = {t="quest",n="Save Techbot's Brain!",z="gnomeregan",s="Tinkmaster Overspark sends you into Gnomeregan to save Techbot's Brain! and recover its memory core. The machine once aided researchers, but radiation filled the city and an electrical surge during its fall polarized its brain and made its behavior violent. Overspark hopes the core will help him reverse the damage and restore his creation.",h="Tinkmaster Overspark sends you into Gnomeregan to save Techbot's Brain!",sec={{t="A Mind Inverted",b="Before Gnomeregan fell, Techbot aided researchers with its devices and deep technical knowledge. Tinkmaster Overspark designed the mechanical assistant, and its built-in gizmos made it a marvel of gnomish ingenuity. Then the trogg invasion brought chaos, and toxic radiation filled the city. A stray electrical surge jolted Techbot's delicate workings and polarized its positronic brain into a volatile negatronic state.",sp=0},{t="Salvage Operation",b="Tinkmaster Overspark needs you to recover Techbot's core, for the machine now wanders Gnomeregan's contaminated halls in a frenzy and attacks anyone in sight. Overspark refuses to abandon his prized assistant as scrap. He asks you to find the machine, remove its memory core from the metal chassis, and bring it to Ironforge. With the core, he hopes to understand the polarization and repair Techbot's mind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Techbot?",a="Techbot is a mechanical assistant designed by Tinkmaster Overspark. Before Gnomeregan fell, it helped the Tinkmaster and his associates with its deep knowledge and built-in gizmos.",al={"what is techbot","techbot lore","overspark techbot"},it="target"},{q="Why did Techbot become hostile?",a="A stray electrical spark jolted Techbot's positronic brain during Gnomeregan's fall. The shock reversed its neural alignment into a negatronic state and turned its helpful nature violent.",al={"why is techbot mad","what happened to techbot","techbot polarization"},it="hostile"},{q="Where can Techbot be found?",a="Techbot wanders Gnomeregan's outer corridors and staging halls, beyond the perimeter where exiled gnomes and dwarven expeditionary forces operate.",al={"where is techbot","techbot location","find techbot"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who gives this quest?",a="Tinkmaster Overspark asks you from Tinker Town in Ironforge. There, he oversees salvage and research for High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque.",al={"who starts save techbots brain","overspark location"},it="identity"},{q="Can Techbot truly be repaired?",a="Tinkmaster Overspark believes Techbot's memory core will help him find the cause of its negatronic polarization and restore the machine to working order.",al={"is techbot fixed","can you fix techbot","does techbot survive"}},{q="What happens after returning the memory core?",a="When Overspark receives the core, he begins preparing to dismantle and reconfigure the inverted circuits. Finding the right tools in his cluttered workshop is a challenge of its own.",al={"techbot quest conclusion","turn in techbot core"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Tinkmaster Overspark want Techbot's brain saved?",a="Techbot is Tinkmaster Overspark's prized creation, once serving him and his fellow inventors with an immense archive of knowledge and practical gizmos. When Gnomeregan fell, an errant electrical surge polarized the automaton's positronic brain into a negatronic state, driving it mad. Overspark refuses to abandon his creation and hopes studying the core will let him undo the damage and restore his assistant.",al={"overspark motive","why save techbot","why does overspark want techbot"},it="motive",add="e9c625cc"},{q="What is Techbot's Memory Core for?",a="The memory core houses Techbot's digitized mind and accumulated knowledge. Because the automaton's positronic brain inverted during the fall of Gnomeregan, extracting this component is the only way to inspect the polarity shift and attempt to reprogram or rebuild the mechanical assistant.",al={"techbot memory core","what is memory core for","techbots memory core"},it="item",add="6f8a4042"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you know Gnomeregan was your home city. Techbot shows how its loss damaged even the city's finest intellectual creations.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see in Techbot's shift from positronic to negatronic how catastrophe can warp complex computational matrices.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you help support the gnomish refugees sheltering in Ironforge by recovering lost technology from Gnomeregan's contaminated perimeter."},kw={"gnomeregan","memory core","negatronic","overspark","positronic","techbot","tinker town"},rel={"quest:2923","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Tinkmaster Overspark",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=2922,ri={"Techbot's Memory Core"}},src={"Save Techbot's Brain!"}}
E["quest:2923"] = {t="quest",n="Tinkmaster Overspark",z="gnomeregan",s="In Stormwind, Brother Sarno hears that Techbot has failed and that Tinkmaster Overspark grieves in Ironforge. He sends Alliance adventurers to Tinker Town, where Overspark asks for help recovering Techbot's memory core from Gnomeregan.",h="In Stormwind, Brother Sarno hears that Techbot has failed and that Tinkmaster Overspark grieves in Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Plea from the Cathedral",b="Brother Sarno tends to travelers in Stormwind City and speaks of trouble among the gnomish refugees. Tinkmaster Overspark, one of the minds behind Gnomeregan's wonders, grieves over Techbot's corruption. The mechanical servant once aided the tinkerers faithfully. Then the city fell into ruin.",sp=0},{t="To Tinker Town",b="You take the Deeprun Tram from Stormwind to Ironforge's Tinker Town. There, Overspark seeks adventurers willing to help in Gnomeregan's irradiated halls. He asks them to salvage what remains of Techbot's faculties before the construct causes irreparable harm.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Tinkmaster Overspark?",a="Tinkmaster Overspark is a gnome engineer who trains gnomish engineering. He is in Tinker Town in Ironforge, coordinating efforts to reclaim Gnomeregan and rescue stray gnomish technology from the ruined capital.",al={"overspark","who is overspark","tinkmaster overspark"},it="identity"},{q="Who starts this quest?",a="Brother Sarno, a human cleric in Stormwind City, sends you to help the gnomes in Ironforge.",al={"quest giver","where to get tinkmaster overspark quest"},gp=true},{q="What is Techbot?",a="Techbot is a mechanical creation designed by Tinkmaster Overspark. It once served gnomish engineers as a helpful tool, but malfunctioned after Gnomeregan fell and went rogue in the irradiated city.",al={"techbot","what happened to techbot"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Tinkmaster Overspark be found?",a="Tinkmaster Overspark is in Tinker Town, the gnomish quarter in Ironforge's eastern district, among fellow refugee tinkerers and experimental machinery.",al={"overspark location","where is overspark"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What follows after speaking to Overspark?",a="After you speak with Overspark, he asks you to enter Gnomeregan, deactivate Techbot, and retrieve its memory core so it can be restored.",al={"next quest","save techbot's brain"},it="next_step"},{q="Why is the Alliance interested in an inventor's broken machine?",a="The Alliance cares about the exiled gnomes, and rogue automatons in Gnomeregan threaten expeditions trying to reclaim the underground capital or guard Dun Morogh's borders.",al={"why care about techbot","techbot importance"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why does Brother Sarno send you to Tinkmaster Overspark?",a="Brother Sarno remembers Techbot as a helpful, gentle automaton that faithfully served the gnomes before Gnomeregan fell into chaos. Hearing that Overspark is distraught over his creation's malfunction troubles the holy man. Hoping the machine can still be salvaged rather than left to rot or destruction, Sarno directs sympathetic adventurers to Tinker Town so the distraught tinkmaster can get the help he desperately needs.",al={"why does brother sarno care","brother sarno motive","why send to overspark"},it="motive",add="9c70ad2e"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, each creation you salvage and memory core you recover preserves a piece of your fallen homeland from radiation and troggs.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can learn from the cutting edge of gnomish ingenuity by examining Overspark's rogue creations.",["faction:Alliance"]="As a member of the Alliance, helping the displaced gnomes in Tinker Town strengthens the bonds between Stormwind and the dwarven and gnomish kingdoms."},kw={"gnomeregan","ironforge","overspark","sarno","techbot","tinker town","tinkmaster"},rel={"npc:brother-sarno","quest:2922","subzone:tinker-town","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome"},m={start="Brother Sarno",["end"]="Tinkmaster Overspark",level="26",faction="Alliance",id=2923},src={"Tinkmaster Overspark (quest)"}}
E["quest:2924"] = {t="quest",n="Essential Artificials",z="gnomeregan",s="In Ironforge, Klockmort Spannerspan lacks the components his experiments need. Exiled gnomes fled Gnomeregan during the trogg invasion and radiation disaster, leaving essential artificials in the city's lower halls.",h="In Ironforge, Klockmort Spannerspan lacks the components his experiments need.",sec={{t="Forgotten in the Exodus",b="When troggs overran Gnomeregan and radiation filled its corridors, the gnomes fled with only what they could reach. Essential artificials remained behind. These specialized mechanical parts work in nearly any device, and tinkers and crafters prize them. Now in Ironforge's Tinker Town, master tinker Klockmort Spannerspan cannot continue his new experiments without a supply.",sp=0},{t="Delving the Extrapolators",b="Deep inside Gnomeregan, the components rest in heavy, steam-powered containers called artificial extrapolators. To reach them, you cross irradiated halls where mutated leper gnomes, malfunctioning defense automatons, and feral troggs roam. Klockmort needs twelve components to continue his work, keeping gnomish invention moving through exile.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is an essential artificial?",a="An essential artificial is a mechanical component made by gnomish engineers that works in nearly any device. Tinkers and smiths value these parts as building blocks for complex contraptions and experimental machinery.",al={"what are essential artificials","essential artificial","what is it"},it="item"},{q="Who gives the quest Essential Artificials?",a="Klockmort Spannerspan, a gnomish engineer in Ironforge's Tinker Town, asks for the components.",al={"quest giver","who starts this","where do i get essential artificials"},it="identity"},{q="Where are the essential artificials found in Gnomeregan?",a="The essential artificials are kept deep in Gnomeregan, inside artificial extrapolators scattered through the lower halls. These are tall, steam-powered storage cabinets.",al={"where are they","extrapolator location","how to find artificials"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why were they left behind in Gnomeregan?",a="Troggs invaded Gnomeregan, and radiation flooded the city. During the sudden evacuation, the gnomes left stocks of essential artificials in the lower workshops.",al={"why left behind","why are they in gnomeregan","lore of the artificials"},it="history"},{q="What does Klockmort need them for?",a="Klockmort Spannerspan needs the components for complex experiments he is preparing in his Ironforge workshop.",al={"why does klockmort want them","klockmort's plan"},it="motive"},{q="Is Klockmort's Essentials required before taking this quest?",a="Klockmort's Essentials introduces you to Klockmort and points you to his workshop. You can accept this assignment without completing it.",al={"prerequisite","prereq","klockmorts essentials required"},gp=true},{q="Why does Klockmort need outside adventurers to enter Gnomeregan?",a="Gnomeregan is no longer a functioning city—it is a lethal, irradiated warzone overrun by troggs and deranged leper gnomes. Gnomish tinkers like Klockmort Spannerspan are researchers, not frontline soldiers, and the surviving gnomes in Tinker Town are refugees living on dwarven hospitality rather than an invading army. Venturing into the deepest, most dangerous sectors of the ruined city requires seasoned adventurers capable of fighting through waves of hostile mutants to reach the storage containers.",al={"why send me","why adventurers","why cant klockmort get them"},it="why_me",add="41f0ee2b"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, recovering these components helps preserve your people's craft and invention during exile in Ironforge.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know how much work can halt for want of one part. These components show the skill of Gnomeregan's engineers before the city fell.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, helping the exiled gnomes recover their lost technology strengthens the Alliance's engineering base in Ironforge."},kw={"artificial extrapolator","essential artificials","gnomeregan","gnomish engineering","ironforge","klockmort spannerspan","tinker town"},rel={"quest:1704","quest:2925","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge"},m={start="Klockmort Spannerspan",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=2924,ri={"Essential Artificial"}},src={"Essential Artificials"}}
E["quest:2925"] = {t="quest",n="Klockmort's Essentials",z="gnomeregan",s="In Darnassus, Mathiel carries Klockmort Spannerspan's urgent plea across the sea. Bound to his post, he asks Alliance travelers to find his gnome friend in Ironforge.",h="In Darnassus, Mathiel carries Klockmort Spannerspan's urgent plea across the sea.",sec={{t="A Call Across Continents",b="From the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus, Mathiel sends word to Dun Morogh. Klockmort Spannerspan needs bold allies for a venture into Gnomeregan, but Mathiel cannot leave his post to travel there. So he asks capable Alliance travelers passing through Darnassus to make the journey in his place.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Tinkertown",b="Klockmort Spannerspan works in Tinkertown, Ironforge's district for gnomes driven from their underground city. He plans to recover vital machinery from Gnomeregan's contaminated corridors. Mathiel's referral brings you to Klockmort's workshop, where he needs help reclaiming what was left behind.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest Klockmort's Essentials?",a="Mathiel gives the summons. The night elf cannot leave his post for Ironforge, so he asks trusted Alliance travelers to answer his longtime friend Klockmort Spannerspan's plea.",al={"quest giver","who starts klockmort essentials","mathiel quest"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I find Klockmort Spannerspan?",a="Find Klockmort Spannerspan in Tinkertown, Ironforge's gnomish district. Gnomes displaced from their lost home have set up workshops and equipment there.",al={"where is klockmort","klockmort location","klockmort spannerspan ironforge"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Klockmort need help in Gnomeregan?",a="Klockmort needs help retrieving essential mechanical components from Gnomeregan. Toxic fallout overran the city, and its ruins hold troggs, deranged leper gnomes, and haywire automata.",al={"what does klockmort want","why gnomeregan mission","klockmort purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Is this quest required to enter Gnomeregan?",a="No. Mathiel's summons leads you to Klockmort Spannerspan, but you can speak with him in Ironforge and accept his assignments without the introduction.",al={"is this quest mandatory","prereq for gnomeregan","can i skip klockmort essentials"},gp=true},{q="What quest follows Klockmort's Essentials?",a="After you speak with Klockmort Spannerspan, he directs you to Essential Artificials. It sends you deep inside Gnomeregan.",al={"next quest","followup","essential artificials followup"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why is Mathiel interested in helping a gnome in Ironforge?",a="Mathiel and Klockmort are longtime personal friends. Though stationed far away and unable to leave his post, Mathiel seeks someone trustworthy to help his friend.",al={"mathiel connection","why does mathiel care","mathiel and klockmort"},it="motive"},{q="Why does Mathiel ask you to go instead of going himself?",a="Mathiel is bound by duty to remain at his post in Darnassus, unable to travel across the sea to Dun Morogh. Though his heart aches to aid his friend Klockmort directly, he must rely on an able adventurer travelling toward Ironforge to answer the call in his stead.",al={"why cant mathiel go","why send me mathiel","why doesnt mathiel help klockmort"},it="why_me",add="b4ad922f"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you carry Mathiel's appeal from Darnassus to Klockmort in Ironforge. Night elf lands and dwarven halls join in common defense.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you know every call to Tinkertown aids the ongoing struggle to reclaim your lost home of Gnomeregan."},kw={"essential artificials","gnomeregan","ironforge","klockmort spannerspan","klockmort's essentials","leper gnomes","mathiel","tinkertown"},rel={"quest:1703","quest:2924","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome"},m={start="Mathiel",["end"]="Klockmort Spannerspan",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=2925},src={"Klockmort's Essentials"}}
E["quest:2926"] = {t="quest",n="Gnogaine",z="gnomeregan",s="In Kharanos, Ozzie Togglevolt sends adventurers toward Gnomeregan to gather radioactive fallout. He hopes to make a cure for the leper gnomes, though the brew may become potent drink.",h="In Kharanos, Ozzie Togglevolt sends adventurers toward Gnomeregan to gather radioactive fallout.",sec={{t="A Cure or a Cocktail",b="Since Gnomeregan fell, refugees such as Gnoarn have sought to kill the trogg invaders and reverse the sickness that changed their kin. Ozzie Togglevolt and his partner Razzle Sprysprocket have taken another path from their workshop in Kharanos. Ozzie says they are trying to make a cure for the leper gnomes. Their formula might instead become very strong rum.",sp=0},{t="Harvesting the Glow",b="Ozzie and Razzle need toxic residue from the heart of the disaster. Ozzie gives adventurers a leaden collection phial and sends them toward Gnomeregan's breached tunnels. Irradiated Invaders and Irradiated Pillagers roam there, troggs saturated with leaking waste. The phial needs their green glow.",sp=0},{t="Hair and High Hopes",b="With a full phial of green glow, Ozzie prepares a live trial. He hopes the brew will restore the health and sanity of a captured leper gnome. He also hopes the fallout mixture might cure his baldness.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who offers the quest Gnogaine?",a="Ozzie Togglevolt, a gnome tinkerer in Kharanos, offers this work.",al={"who gives gnogaine","gnogaine quest giver","ozzie togglevolt quest"},it="identity",gp=true},{q="What do I need to collect for this quest?",a="Use an Empty Leaden Collection Phial on glowing Irradiated Invaders or Irradiated Pillagers to gather radioactive fallout until the phial is full.",al={"gnogaine objective","what do i collect gnogaine","full leaden collection phial"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Where can I find the irradiated troggs?",a="Find the irradiated troggs in the outer entrance caverns and winding halls leading to Gnomeregan's instance portal. You can reach them without entering the dungeon.",al={"where are irradiated troggs","gnogaine trogg location","irradiated invader location"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Do I have to complete 'The Day After' before taking this quest?",a="No. Ozzie offers this independently of The Day After, though that story is tied to the situation in Kharanos and leads up to it.",al={"is the day after required","gnogaine prerequisite"},gp=true},{q="What is Ozzie trying to accomplish with the radioactive fallout?",a="Ozzie and Razzle are trying to make a cure for leper gnomes, though Ozzie admits the brew might become high-proof rum.",al={"why does ozzie want radiation","what is gnogaine for"},it="motive"},{q="What quest follows Gnogaine?",a="A full phial leads to The Only Cure is More Green Glow, which sends you deeper into Gnomeregan.",al={"gnogaine follow up","what comes after gnogaine"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Full Leaden Collection Phial for?",a="The phial is shielded with lead to safely store and transport the dangerous, glowing radioactive fallout extracted from troggs around Gnomeregan. Ozzie Togglevolt and Razzle Sprysprocket need that concentrated radioactive matter as a vital ingredient for their experimental concoction, which they hope will either cure their afflicted leper gnome captive, brew an extraordinarily potent rum, or perhaps regrow Ozzie's hair.",al={"full leaden collection phial use","why leaden phial","leaden collection phial purpose"},it="item",add="28ada800"},{q="What are the irradiated troggs in Gnomeregan?",a="The troggs originally erupted from deep beneath Gnomeregan, overrunning the technological marvel of a city. In a desperate attempt to eradicate the invasion, High Tinker Mekkatorque and his advisors flooded the lower corridors with toxic radiation. Instead of dying off, many troggs survived, mutating into vicious irradiated invaders and pillagers that now brim with a sickly green, radioactive glow.",al={"irradiated invaders","irradiated pillagers","why are troggs irradiated"},it="target",add="dfd2dab8"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As an exiled gnome, you know how desperate your kin are to find a remedy for their irradiated brethren. Even Ozzie's wild experiments are worth trying.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you know Gnomeregan's contamination threatens all of Dun Morogh. Understanding or containing the fallout matters to the region's safety.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you see gnomish field science at work: raw radioactive runoff gathered in shielded leaden phials."},kw={"gnoarn","gnogaine","gnomeregan","green glow","irradiated trogg","kharanos","leper gnome","ozzie togglevolt","phial","radiation"},rel={"npc:ozzie-togglevolt","quest:2927","quest:2962","zone:gnomeregan","subzone:kharanos","topic:leper-gnome","topic:trogg","topic:gnome"},m={start="Ozzie Togglevolt",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=2926,ri={"Full Leaden Collection Phial"}},src={"Gnogaine"}}
E["quest:2927"] = {t="quest",n="The Day After",z="gnomeregan",s="In Ironforge and Kharanos, Gnomeregan's survivors search for an answer to their city's ruin. Gnoarn sends travelers to Ozzie Togglevolt, who studies the contamination and hopes to find a solution.",h="In Ironforge and Kharanos, Gnomeregan's survivors search for an answer to their city's ruin.",sec={{t="A Tragic Loss",b="In Ironforge's Tinker Town, Gnoarn mourns Gnomeregan and the loss of his gnomefro. Trogg invaders took the mechanical city, and toxic fallout stripped away his prized mane. Fury toward the troggs and hope of reclaiming the city move him to send sympathetic travelers to colleagues who can salvage what remains.",sp=0},{t="The Road to Kharanos",b="In Kharanos, inventive gnomes have begun to face the fallout. Gnoarn sends travelers to Ozzie Togglevolt, who works with his partner Razzle Sprysprocket. Ozzie remembers the catastrophe, when Gnoarn's locks fell out in clumps and madness and thirst for vengeance took hold. Now Ozzie studies the contamination in the snowbound town, using his engineering skill to seek an antidote.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Gnoarn?",a="Gnoarn is a gnome refugee in Tinker Town, Ironforge. The trogg invaders and radioactive vent catastrophe have embittered him, and he is especially shaken by the sudden loss of his once-proud gnomefro.",al={"gnoarn","bald gnome","who gives the day after"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Gnoarn send you to Ozzie Togglevolt?",a="Gnoarn hopes Gnomeregan can still be saved. Ozzie Togglevolt and his partner Razzle Sprysprocket are in Kharanos, studying the toxic radiation clinging to the city and trying to engineer a cure.",al={"why go to ozzie","ozzie togglevolt quest","kharanos engineer"},it="purpose"},{q="What happened to Gnomeregan to cause this?",a="During a vast trogg invasion beneath the city, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque was persuaded to vent radioactive toxic waste into the lower halls to destroy them. The plan failed. Countless gnomes were killed or mutated, Gnomeregan became unlivable, and the troggs survived.",al={"what happened to gnomeregan","why is gnomeregan irradiated","trogg invasion"},it="history"},{q="Where does this quest chain lead after reaching Ozzie?",a="After you report to Ozzie, he asks you to gather radioactive fallout from irradiated troggs outside Gnomeregan. He will test experimental mixtures meant to neutralize it.",al={"the day after follow up","what comes after the day after","next quest"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Gnoarn want this done?",a="Gnoarn is fueled by personal fury and stubborn hope. The radioactive fallout that ruined Gnomeregan also stripped him of his pride and joy: the only gnomefro in all of Azeroth. Bitter over his baldness and burning for revenge against the invading troggs, he refuses to give up on his home. He believes that by directing able adventurers to Ozzie Togglevolt, there is still a chance to reverse the disaster and reclaim the city.",al={"gnoarn motive","why help gnoarn","why does gnoarn care"},it="motive",add="b3abdd6a"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you know Gnoarn's lament. It carries the tragedy, eccentric pride, and bitter vengeance of refugees driven from their capital.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance hero, you help Dun Morogh's gnomish thinkers contain the bizarre biochemical disaster threatening the mountain realm.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you see Ozzie Togglevolt testing ideas while gnomish tinkerers confront a runaway technological disaster."},kw={"gnoarn","gnomefro","gnomeregan","kharanos","ozzie togglevolt","radiation leak","the day after","troggs"},rel={"npc:gnoarn","npc:ozzie-togglevolt","quest:2926","quest:2962","zone:gnomeregan","subzone:kharanos","topic:trogg"},m={start="Gnoarn",["end"]="Ozzie Togglevolt",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=2927},src={"The Day After"}}
E["quest:2928"] = {t="quest",n="Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators",z="gnomeregan",s="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, Shoni the Shilent readies tunneling machines for Dun Morogh. Short on parts, she sends you into Gnomeregan to salvage them from rogue automatons.",h="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, Shoni the Shilent readies tunneling machines for Dun Morogh.",sec={{t="A Fleet in Need of Guts",b="In Stormwind's Dwarven District, Shoni the Shilent prepares gyrodrillmatic excavationators for Dun Morogh. Gnomish engineers there aid their displaced kin. The machines will carry people and supplies underground, but these massive rigs cannot work without the mechanical parts Shoni lacks.",sp=0},{t="Salvage in the Fallen City",b="Gnomeregan once supplied gnomish high technology. Its ruined halls and nearby tunnels still hold machines worth salvaging, though malfunctioning defense bots, mechanical sentries, and clockwork laborers roam unchecked. Shoni sends you into the fallen city for two dozen bundles of robo-mechanical guts, to bring back to human lands.",sp=0},{t="A Monumental Undertaking",b="Two dozen bundles of mechanical guts provide enough scrap to repair one excavationator. Shoni still has nearly four hundred machines to prepare, so mass transport underground remains a slow undertaking. Each working machine is a small step toward regaining ground lost in Gnomeregan's fall.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is a gyrodrillmatic excavationator?",a="A gyrodrillmatic excavationator is a heavy gnomish tunneling rig, also called a mole machine, built to dig and carry people or supplies underground. Shoni the Shilent is preparing a fleet to serve Dun Morogh.",al={"gyrodrillmatic excavationators","what is excavationator","gnome drill"}},{q="Who is Shoni the Shilent?",a="Shoni the Shilent is a gnomish engineer in Stormwind's Dwarven District. Outspoken and demanding, she is preparing hundreds of mechanical diggers.",al={"shoni the shilent","shoni","who is shoni"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Shoni need parts from Gnomeregan specifically?",a="Gnomeregan once supplied gnomish high technology, and its fallen halls hold haywire automatons, clockwork servitors, and defensive mechs. The city's manufacturing supply lines are severed, so these rogue machines offer compatible gnomish spare parts.",al={"why gnomeregan parts","why robot guts","gnomeregan salvage"},it="why_here"},{q="Where are the Robo-Mechanical Guts found?",a="Robo-Mechanical Guts can be salvaged from mechanical sentries, clockwork constructs, and other hostile machines in Gnomeregan's ruined facility and upper tunnel approaches.",al={"robo-mechanical guts","where to get guts","mechanical guts gnomeregan"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Does fixing one machine finish Shoni's fleet?",a="No. Two dozen bundles of mechanical guts repair one drill. Shoni says she still has 398 excavationators left to go.",al={"how many excavationators","shoni fleet size","how many drills"}},{q="Why is an excavation fleet being prepared for Dun Morogh?",a="Dun Morogh is the gnomes' ancestral home and the site of their fallen capital. Heavy tunneling rigs can help dig, clear debris, and support work in the snow-covered mountain reaches.",al={"fleet to dun morogh","why dun morogh","excavators purpose"},it="motive"},{q="What are the Robo-Mechanical Guts used for?",a="Shoni the Shilent needs them as salvaged internal components to repair her fleet of gyrodrillmatic excavationators. The complex engineering of these subterranean tunneling vehicles requires precision gears, wiring, and actuators that are difficult to forge from scratch in Stormwind. By stripping functioning innards from the autonomous clockwork machines roaming Gnomeregan, she can salvage the vital spare parts needed to bring her grounded drilling rigs back online.",al={"what are robo-mechanical guts for","robo mechanical guts use","shoni guts use"},it="item",add="b2dc5b24"},{q="What are you fighting inside Gnomeregan for Shoni?",a="You are sent to dismantle the rogue bots and mechs wandering the irradiated halls and outskirts of Gnomeregan. When the subterranean gnomish capital fell to the trogg invasion and radioactive fallout, countless automated defense systems and utility contraptions malfunctioned, turning hostile to outsiders. Shoni sees these abandoned, roaming automatons not just as hazards, but as an open field of scrap waiting to be scavenged.",al={"who do i fight for shoni","gnomeregan targets guts","what machines have guts"},it="target",add="1cb24930"},{q="Why does Shoni need you to gather the parts instead of going herself?",a="Shoni is an engineer stationed in the Dwarven District of Stormwind, occupied with maintaining machinery and overseeing the assembly of a massive excavation fleet. Venturing deep into an irradiated, trogg-infested ruin overrun with lethal clockwork sentries requires an armed adventurer willing to fight through hazardous corridors. She stays behind to inspect the salvage and repair the rigs as components arrive.",al={"why send me for guts","why doesnt shoni go herself","why me shoni quest"},it="why_me",add="33a01105"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, each salvaged component brings Shoni's underground fleet closer to working order. From Stormwind, the dream of reclamation and industrial recovery lives on.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, stripping precise clockwork innards from Gnomeregan's fallen servitors offers a practical lesson in gnomish design and heavy machinery repair.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, helping gnomes prepare excavation machines in Stormwind strengthens ties between their human hosts and the exiled survivors working to reclaim their heritage."},kw={"dun morogh","dwarven district","excavationators","gnomeregan","gnomish engineering","gyrodrillmatic","robo-mechanical guts","shoni the shilent"},rel={"npc:shoni-the-shilent","zone:gnomeregan","zone:dunmorogh","topic:stormwind-kingdom"},m={start="Shoni the Shilent",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=2928,ri={"Robo-Mechanical Guts"}},src={"Gyrodrillmatic Excavationators"}}
E["quest:2930"] = {t="quest",n="Data Rescue",z="gnomeregan",s="Master Mechanic Castpipe sends you into Gnomeregan to recover its records. Troggs and radiation drove the gnomes from the city, but the punchograph terminals still guard its archives behind layers of clearance.",h="Master Mechanic Castpipe sends you into Gnomeregan to recover its records.",sec={{t="Lost Archives of the Underground",b="Troggs and radiation drove Gnomeregan's people from the city, leaving centuries of research, schematics, and civic records behind. Matrix Punchograph terminals still line its technological corridors. They manage security clearance and store files. Master Mechanic Castpipe in Ironforge's Tinker Town wants you to recover those punch-encoded archives from the city's depths.",sp=0},{t="A Hierarchy of Perforations",b="Gnomish mainframes demand clearance in stages. First, find a White Punch Card among the wreckage outside the inner gates. Insert it into the Matrix Punchograph 3005-A in the Train Depot to make a Yellow card. Then take that to the 3005-B terminal in the Dormitory for a Blue card. Model 3005-C advances it to Red. The final terminal, 3005-D, waits in the Engineering Labs, where the Red card becomes a Prismatic Punch Card.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Levity in Binary",b="Gnomeregan's punch cards carry technical records and more. Their binary patterns also hold humorous quips, workplace complaints, and off-color jokes about High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque wearing night elven undergarments. Even the city's computing guilds could not resist a practical joke.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Prismatic Punch Card?",a="The Prismatic Punch Card is the highest security tier recognized by Gnomeregan's automated mainframes. Matrix Punchograph 3005-D in the Engineering Labs creates it from a Red Punch Card.",al={"prismatic card","what is punch card","gnomeregan punch card"},it="item"},{q="Where does the sequence of punch cards begin?",a="The sequence begins with a White Punch Card salvaged from troggs and mechanical derelicts outside the main entrance, near the Train Depot.",al={"where to get white punch card","how to start punch cards","first punch card"},gp=true},{q="Where are the Matrix Punchograph terminals located?",a="Matrix Punchograph 3005-A is in the Train Depot outside the entrance. Model 3005-B is inside the Dormitory past the Clean Zone, and 3005-C is on the catwalk platforms beyond. Model 3005-D is on the lower level of the Engineering Labs.",al={"terminal locations","where are punchographs","punch card machines"},gp=true},{q="Who is Master Mechanic Castpipe?",a="Master Mechanic Castpipe is a senior gnome engineer among the refugees in Ironforge's Tinker Town. He coordinates efforts to recover Gnomeregan's intellectual heritage from the fallen capital.",al={"castpipe","who gives data rescue","castpipe lore"},it="identity"},{q="What data is actually on the cards?",a="The cards hold critical computational data, gnomish engineering banter, lighthearted jokes about regional leaders like Thrall and Mekkatorque, and eccentric notes.",al={"card text","binary translation","what does the binary say"}},{q="Can Horde players access these terminals?",a="Master Mechanic Castpipe offers this work only to the Alliance in Ironforge. Anyone carrying the required cards can use the punchograph terminals inside the dungeon.",al={"horde data rescue","horde punch cards","can horde use terminals"},gp=true},{q="Why does Master Mechanic Castpipe want the punch card recovered?",a="When the gnomes evacuated Gnomeregan during its fall, mountains of vital operational and technical data were left behind in the chaos. Master Mechanic Castpipe considers the information stored in the high-security Matrix Punchograph terminals critical to the gnomes' survival and rebuilding efforts, insisting they cannot afford to lose it permanently.",al={"castpipe motive","why does castpipe need punch card","why data rescue"},it="motive",add="0f0753b5"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you help reclaim your people's heritage by recovering Gnomeregan's data. Each salvaged punch card preserves your city's ingenuity from troggs and radiation.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can study how the Matrix Punchograph network stores data and uses intricate clearance mechanisms devised by the Tinkers' Court.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you support the displaced gnomish government in Ironforge by helping Castpipe. Your aid strengthens unity and technological capabilities among the Grand Alliance."},kw={"castpipe","data rescue","engineering labs","gnomeregan","matrix punchograph","prismatic punch card","punch card","tinker town","train depot"},rel={"quest:2931","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome","subzone:train-depot","subzone:dormitory","subzone:engineering-labs","subzone:clean-zone"},m={start="Master Mechanic Castpipe",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=2930,ri={"Prismatic Punch Card"}},src={"Data Rescue"}}
E["quest:2931"] = {t="quest",n="Castpipe's Task",z="gnomeregan",s="In Ironforge, Master Mechanic Castpipe calls travelers to recover Gnomeregan's records. The ruined halls still hold vital mechanical and technical knowledge.",h="In Ironforge, Master Mechanic Castpipe calls travelers to recover Gnomeregan's records.",sec={{t="A Call to Tinkertown",b="After Gnomeregan fell and was sealed under radioactive quarantine, its surviving gnomes found refuge in Ironforge's Tinkertown. Troggs and irradiated constructs still overrun their old home. Deep within the city, computing arrays hold operational records and mechanical schematics. Castpipe seeks outsiders willing to brave the toxic halls and recover files that may explain what went wrong or help the gnomes return.",sp=0},{t="Assembly Endorsement",b="Gaxim Rustfizzle of the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences spreads word of Castpipe's effort. Castpipe belongs to no academic body, yet his fellow gnomes respect his skill and support his work. Rustfizzle puts the operation's strategic value at an eighty-four percent chance. Travelers can report to Tinkertown for orders.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Master Mechanic Castpipe?",a="Master Mechanic Castpipe is a respected gnomish engineer in Tinkertown, Ironforge. He organizes salvage teams to recover data from the underground ruins of Gnomeregan.",al={"castpipe","who is castpipe","master mechanic castpipe"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Castpipe want data from Gnomeregan?",a="When Gnomeregan was contaminated and evacuated, its mainframe memory was left with critical technical knowledge, blueprints and internal system logs. The displaced gnomes need this information as they hope to rebuild.",al={"gnomeregan data","why retrieve data","gnomeregan records"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who is Gaxim Rustfizzle?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle is a gnome scholar with the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences. He supports Castpipe's recovery effort and directs capable travelers to it.",al={"gaxim","rustfizzle"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Castpipe be found?",a="Master Mechanic Castpipe can be found in Tinkertown, the gnome-settled district in Ironforge's eastern quarter.",al={"castpipe location","where is castpipe"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Castpipe?",a="Reporting to Master Mechanic Castpipe leads to Data Rescue inside the fallen city. Travelers enter Gnomeregan's contaminated interior to recover computer punch cards and storage media.",al={"next quest","what comes next","after castpipe"},it="next_step"},{q="What is the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences?",a="The Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences is a respected gnomish society devoted to scientific, magical and mechanical study. Members such as Gaxim Rustfizzle use probability to assess important work.",al={"the assembly","enlightened assembly"},it="people"},{q="Why does Gaxim Rustfizzle send you to Master Mechanic Castpipe?",a="Gaxim Rustfizzle respects Master Mechanic Castpipe's intellect, even if Castpipe lacks membership in the Enlightened Assembly of Arcanology, Alchemy and Engineering Sciences. By Gaxim's calculations, there is an eighty-four percent chance that whatever data retrieval operation Castpipe is preparing in Gnomeregan is genuinely vital to the gnomes. Given those favorable odds, Gaxim is eager to direct capable adventurers toward Ironforge to support the reclamation effort.",al={"why does gaxim send you","gaxim rustfizzle motive","why talk to castpipe"},it="motive",add="0652d792"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you help preserve a piece of your fallen home from radiation and destruction with each recovery effort. Castpipe's work touches your people's survival.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know Gnomeregan's data cores hold computational marvels and advanced schematics unmatched elsewhere on Azeroth.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an ally of the Alliance, you support displaced gnomes as they secure their lost archives. That work strengthens Tinkertown and the Alliance's technological standing."},kw={"assembly","castpipe","data rescue","gaxim","gnomeregan","ironforge","rustfizzle","tinkertown"},rel={"quest:2930","npc:gaxim-rustfizzle","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome"},m={start="Gaxim Rustfizzle",["end"]="Master Mechanic Castpipe",level="28",faction="Alliance",id=2931},src={"Castpipe's Task"}}
E["quest:2945"] = {t="quest",n="Grime-Encrusted Ring",z="gnomeregan",s="A Dark Iron dwarf in Gnomeregan carries a ring caked in toxic filth and hardened muck. The Sparklematic 5200 in the Clean Zone dormitory can scour it clean and reveal its markings.",h="A Dark Iron dwarf in Gnomeregan carries a ring caked in toxic filth and hardened muck.",sec={{t="A Relic Beneath the Muck",b="Fighting leaves Gnomeregan's corridors coated in toxic sludge, oil, and radioactive fallout. Dark Iron dwarves who infiltrate the city carry trinkets fouled by that filth. One ring bears a crust that ordinary washing cannot remove. Beneath it, the metal may be copper, gold, or junk.",sp=0},{t="The Sparklematic 5200",b="The Sparklematic 5200 in the Clean Zone dormitory takes coins, scours fouled items, and returns them polished and wrapped with a bow. Cleaning the ring reveals a city's seal and initials engraved inside the band. Those markings begin Return of the Ring, a journey toward restitution.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where do you find the Grime-Encrusted Ring?",a="Dark Iron dwarves inside Gnomeregan carry the ring.",al={"ring drop","where does grime ring drop","who drops grime encrusted ring"},gp=true},{q="How do you clean the ring?",a="Take the ring to the Sparklematic 5200 in Gnomeregan's Clean Zone dormitory. Pay the required coin fee, and the machine scours away the hardened muck.",al={"clean ring","how to clean grime encrusted ring","where to wash ring"},gp=true},{q="What happens after the ring is cleaned?",a="The Sparklematic returns the restored ring in a neatly packaged box, with its personal engravings revealed. This begins Return of the Ring, which leads you to seek the ring's original owner.",al={"next quest grime ring","what do i do with clean ring","sparklematic ring result"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Can Horde players complete this quest?",a="Yes. Horde adventurers can clean the ring with the Sparklematic 5200. Later steps send Horde players to an engineer in Orgrimmar instead of back to Ironforge.",al={"is grime ring alliance only","horde grime encrusted ring","can horde clean ring"},gp=true},{q="Why is the ring wrapped in a gift box after cleaning?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 scours away sludge and grime, then packages each cleaned item and ties on a decorative bow, all with gnomish whimsy.",al={"gift wrapped ring","why gift box sparklematic"}},{q="Are there multiple Sparklematic machines?",a="Several Sparklematic units line the wall in the Clean Zone dormitory. Only the one on the left as you enter by the stairs, near the friendly gnomes, works for the ring.",al={"which sparklematic","sparklematic 5200 locations"},gp=true},{q="Why do you need to clean the Grime-Encrusted Ring?",a="When you pry the ring from the fallen Dark Iron dwarf, it is coated in a thick, hardened crust of radioactive sludge and cavern muck. You can catch the faint glimmer of precious metal and a gem beneath the grime, but the caked residue makes it unwearable and impossible to inspect. Cleaning it is the only way to reveal its true craftsmanship and see if it holds any real value or purpose.",al={"why clean the ring","grime encrusted ring purpose","why wash grime encrusted ring"},it="motive",add="5abd59ba"},{q="What is the Grime-Encrusted Ring?",a="It appears to be a valuable piece of jewelry carried into Gnomeregan by one of the invading Dark Iron dwarves. Completely smothered in irradiated industrial filth, its fine metalwork and embedded stone are entirely hidden until fed through Gnomeregan's automated cleaning apparatus, the Sparklematic 5200.",al={"what is grime encrusted ring","grime encrusted ring lore","what kind of ring is it"},it="item",add="c5a1096d"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="The Sparklematic 5200 shows gnomish engineering at work, combining industrial solvent-scrubbing with an automatic gift wrapper.",["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you know that even as your city fell, its inventors built sanitation machines that finish dangerous wash cycles with a cheerful bell and a bow.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you can see that an infiltrating Dark Iron dwarf may have scavenged the ring from Ironforge or from gnomish victims during Gnomeregan's fall."},kw={"clean zone","dark iron","dormitory","gnomeregan","grime-encrusted ring","return of the ring","sparklematic 5200"},rel={"quest:2947","quest:2948","quest:2950","npc:nogg","zone:gnomeregan","topic:gnome"},m={start="Grime-Encrusted Ring",["end"]="Sparklematic 5200",id=2945,ri={"Grime-Encrusted Ring"}},src={"Grime-Encrusted Ring (quest)"}}
E["quest:2947"] = {t="quest",n="Return of the Ring",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, a golden ring bears a maker’s mark that leads you to Ironforge.",h="In Gnomeregan, a golden ring bears a maker’s mark that leads you to Ironforge.",sec={{t="A Sludge-Coated Treasure",b="You place a grime-caked bauble in Gnomeregan’s Sparklematic 5200. The machine strips away years of irradiated grime, revealing a polished Brilliant Gold Ring that still hums with arcane power. Inside the band, three initials, “TdK,” sit beside Ironforge’s hallmark seal.",sp=0},{t="The Artisan of the Mystic Ward",b="Talvash del Kissel, a gnome jeweler in Ironforge’s Mystic Ward, recognizes the ring as one of his standard designs from before Gnomeregan fell. He often fends off imaginary debt collectors while he works. Learning that Dark Iron infiltrators carried the ring unsettles him, and leaves questions about what stirred beneath the lost city.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who made the ring found in Gnomeregan?",a="The initials “TdK” belong to Talvash del Kissel, a gnome jeweler in Ironforge’s Mystic Ward. Before Gnomeregan fell, he ran a jewelry shop there and made several simple magical rings of this design.",al={"who made the ring","ring initials tdk","who is tdk"},it="origin"},{q="Where did the ring originally come from?",a="The ring came from deep within Gnomeregan, where it was found as a grime-encrusted bauble carried by hostile invaders such as the Dark Iron dwarves. The Sparklematic 5200 restored its golden sheen and maker’s marks.",al={"where was ring found","where does ring come from"},it="history"},{q="Why were Dark Iron dwarves carrying Talvash's ring?",a="Talvash is unsure why Dark Iron infiltrators carried his old work. The ring may have come from his abandoned workshop or been taken from someone who failed to escape Gnomeregan’s invasion.",al={"why do dark irons have it","dark iron ring lore"},it="conflict"},{q="Why does Talvash del Kissel think you are his landlord?",a="Talvash is high-strung and eccentric, and often behind on his Ironforge rent. When strangers approach his shop aggressively, he assumes bailiffs or landlords have come to collect his overdue debts.",al={"why is talvash paranoid","talvash rent"},it="identity"},{q="Does Talvash make cursed jewelry?",a="Talvash insists to prospective customers that he does not make cursed items. His nervous denials tend to raise more questions than they settle.",al={"is talvash cursed","cursed jewelry ironforge"}},{q="Can I just keep the ring instead of returning it?",a="The ring has magical properties, but its creator can inspect it and offer to refine its enchantment through further work.",al={"keep the ring","should i return the ring"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why does the Sparklematic 5200 want the ring returned?",a="It doesn't. The Sparklematic 5200 is an automated cleaning device designed to process grime-encrusted salvage pulled from Gnomeregan's depths. It cleans whatever you put into it and spits out the restored object. Once the machine dispenses the polished Brilliant Gold Ring, returning it is entirely your choice after spotting the maker's mark and Ironforge seal stamped inside the band.",al={"why return the ring","sparklematic 5200 motive","why does the machine want the ring returned"},it="motive",add="8e194cce"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, finding lost handiwork in Gnomeregan offers a rare glimpse of the peaceful crafts your people practiced before Thermaplugg’s disaster.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can see the growing threat Emperor Thaurissan’s agents pose to the Alliance’s mountain home in Ironforge-marked artifacts held by Dark Iron dwarves."},kw={"brilliant gold ring","dark iron","ironforge seal","mystic ward","sparklematic","talvash del kissel","tdk"},rel={"npc:talvash-del-kissel","quest:2945","quest:2948","zone:gnomeregan","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome","topic:alliance"},m={start="Sparklematic 5200",["end"]="Talvash del Kissel",faction="Alliance",id=2947},src={"Return of the Ring (Alliance)"}}
E["quest:2949"] = {t="quest",n="Return of the Ring",z="gnomeregan",s="A ring from Gnomeregan bears Orgrimmar's seal and the letters NOG. Its trail leads to Nogg, a goblin engineer with a theory about the ruins.",h="A ring from Gnomeregan bears Orgrimmar's seal and the letters NOG.",sec={{t="A Curious Discovery",b="You clean a ring from Gnomeregan in the Sparklematic 5200. The machine strips away the filth and reveals Orgrimmar's official seal, a surge of magical power, and the partly legible letters NOG. Gnomeregan lies deep in Khaz Modan, an Alliance city far from the Horde capital. The ring may have been made in Kalimdor or carried there on a doomed expedition, but its seal points back to Orgrimmar.",sp=0},{t="Gnomish Rivalries and Dark Iron Plots",b="You take the ring to Nogg in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. The goblin engineer says it is not his, though its origins raise questions. Goblins have long regarded gnomish inventors as eccentric rivals. Nogg suspects the gnomes stole and altered Dark Iron golem designs. Since Dark Iron dwarves held the ring inside Gnomeregan, he thinks they may be seeking payback, a lead worth investigating.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why does a ring found in Gnomeregan bear the seal of Orgrimmar?",a="No one knows exactly how the ring reached Gnomeregan. Dark Iron dwarves carried it deep into the ruins, where it was recovered. Its Orgrimmar seal links it to Horde metalworkers and craftsmen in Durotar.",al={"why orgrimmar seal","horde ring in gnomeregan","how did the ring get there"},it="item"},{q="Who is Nogg?",a="Nogg is a goblin engineer in Orgrimmar's Valley of Honor. He oversees engineering supplies and machines, and his name matches the worn letters on the cleaned ring.",al={"who is nogg","nogg orgrimmar","nog letters ring"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Sparklematic 5200?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 is an automated industrial wash system in Gnomeregan's Clean Zone. It strips heavy layers of toxic sludge and irradiation from objects brought out of the ruined corridors.",al={"what is the sparklematic","sparklematic 5200","cleanomatic"},it="origin"},{q="Does Nogg own the ring?",a="No. Nogg inspects the cleaned ring and says it is not his. He recognizes its craftsmanship and uses his engineering skill to modify it further for you.",al={"is it nogg's ring","did nogg lose his ring","who owns the ring"},sp=1,it="ties"},{q="What does Nogg think happened to Gnomeregan?",a="Nogg suspects the gnomes stole advanced golem blueprints from the Dark Iron clan. He thinks the Dark Irons would want payback and considers the lead worth investigating.",al={"nogg gnomeregan theory","what happened to gnomeregan","why dark iron dwarves"},it="ruin"},{q="Can I keep the ring instead of returning it to Nogg?",a="You can wear the ring at once or take it to Orgrimmar. Bringing it to Nogg lets the goblin engineer inspect its craftsmanship and offer further improvements.",al={"keep brilliant gold ring","should i return the ring","do i have to give it to nogg"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does the Sparklematic 5200 want the ring returned?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 has no will or motive of its own—it is simply an automated cleaning apparatus inside Gnomeregan designed to scrub grime off salvaged objects and spit out whatever comes out. Once it cleans your grime-encrusted ring and dispenses it in a wrapped box, its function is finished. The decision to track down the initials engraved inside the band comes purely from your own curiosity upon discovering the Orgrimmar seal and the partial letters etched within.",al={"sparklematic motive","why return ring sparklematic","sparklematic 5200 goal"},it="motive",add="9392e9ce"}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you rarely find its symbols deep inside the Eastern Kingdoms' leading center of technology. The ring draws you from Khaz Modan to the Valley of Honor.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know goblin inventors in Orgrimmar measure themselves against gnomish invention. Nogg is eager to examine anything recovered from their ruined technological wonder."},kw={"brilliant gold ring","dark iron","gnomeregan","nogg","orgrimmar","return of the ring","sparklematic 5200","valley of honor"},rel={"npc:nogg","zone:gnomeregan","zone:orgrimmar","quest:2945","quest:2950","topic:horde","topic:gnome"},m={start="The Sparklematic 5200",["end"]="Nogg",faction="Horde",id=2949},src={"Return of the Ring (Horde)"}}
E["quest:2951"] = {t="quest",n="The Sparklematic 5200!",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, the Sparklematic 5200! keeps cleaning salvaged valuables for three silver coins. Gnomish ingenuity keeps it working amid the ruined city's chaos.",h="In Gnomeregan, the Sparklematic 5200!",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Grime",b="A pocket of surviving gnomes holds a secure perimeter near the Sparklematic 5200! in Gnomeregan. The machine scrubs harsh subterranean filth from salvaged valuables. Troggs and other subterranean creatures pound on the bulkheads, yet it remains ready for what you bring.",sp=0},{t="Frenzied Operation",b="Place a grime-caked relic and three silver coins in the Sparklematic, and the cleaning begins. The iron machine groans and vibrates, lurching as it strips away toxic sludge, irradiated grease, and rock dust. Moments later, it expels what lay beneath the muck, from precious minerals to mechanical components.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sparklematic 5200?",a="The Sparklematic 5200! is an automated gnomish cleaning machine in a protected pocket of Gnomeregan. It strips radioactive grease, sludge, and dirt from encrusted items recovered in the fallen city.",al={"what does sparklematic 5200 do","sparklematic machine","cleaning machine gnomeregan"},it="identity"},{q="What does the machine require to operate?",a="The Sparklematic needs a Grime-Encrusted Object found among Gnomeregan's monsters and debris, along with three silver coins in its coin slot.",al={"how to use sparklematic","sparklematic cost","what do i put in sparklematic"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why is there an operational machine in the middle of a war zone?",a="Surviving gnomes withdrew to fortified workshops after the trogg invasion and toxic vents devastated Gnomeregan. Machines such as the Sparklematic remained intact and powered there, preserving the convenience of gnomish automated tools.",al={"why is sparklematic here","who put sparklematic in gnomeregan"},it="place"},{q="What comes out after cleaning a grime-encrusted item?",a="The Sparklematic returns the salvaged item cleaned, revealing what lay beneath the muck. That may be trade supplies, crafting stones, gems, or spare engineering parts.",al={"what do you get from sparklematic","sparklematic loot","grime-encrusted object rewards"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Can I use the Sparklematic 5200 more than once?",a="Yes. You can use the Sparklematic repeatedly, bringing more grime-encrusted objects and three silver coins for each cleaning.",al={"is sparklematic repeatable","can i clean multiple grime items","more sparklematic"},gp=true},{q="Why does the machine shake so violently during cleaning?",a="Gnomeregan's encrusted filth is dense, toxic, and hardened. The Sparklematic's agitation and internal scrubbers shear it away, making the chassis lurch and groan.",al={"sparklematic shaking","is sparklematic broken"}},{q="Why does the Sparklematic 5200 want this done?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 is not a sentient being, but an automated gnomish appliance built for a single commercial purpose: cleaning filthy, grime-coated valuables for paying customers. As advertised on its brass plaque, it is engineered to take ruined, muck-covered relics recovered from the contaminated halls of Gnomeregan and scour them clean for three silver coins. It holds no personal agenda beyond fulfilling its programming whenever fed the proper fuel and coin.",al={"why does sparklematic want items","sparklematic 5200 purpose","why feed sparklematic"},it="motive",add="3b5f4e4c"},{q="What is the Grime-Encrusted Object for?",a="A Grime-Encrusted Object is an unidentifiable piece of salvaged gnomish technology, mineral ore, or personal trinket that has been coated in the toxic sludge and radiation flooding Gnomeregan. In its fouled state, the item is completely useless and its true nature remains hidden. Feeding it into the Sparklematic 5200 scrubs away the radioactive muck and caustic buildup, revealing whatever valuable gear, precious gems, or scrap metal lies underneath.",al={"what is grime-encrusted object","grime encrusted object purpose","why keep grime encrusted object"},it="item",add="757f94ef"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see your people's resilience in a cleaning machine that keeps working amid the devastation of their homeland.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can appreciate the motor and sorting mechanism that clean and process unknown debris without jamming or exploding.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can use the Sparklematic to clean salvaged relics in Gnomeregan before carrying them back to Ironforge."},kw={"cleaner","gnome","gnomeregan","grime-encrusted","machine","salvage","sparklematic","sparklematic 5200","trogg"},rel={"quest:2953","zone:gnomeregan","topic:gnome"},m={start="The Sparklematic 5200",faction="Neutral",id=2951,ri={"Grime-Encrusted Object"}},src={"The Sparklematic 5200! (1)"}}
E["quest:2952"] = {t="quest",n="The Sparklematic 5200!",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, the Sparklematic 5200! takes in soiled salvaged objects and cleans them. Its cycles scour away toxic grime, then wrap whatever remains in a gift box.",h="In Gnomeregan, the Sparklematic 5200!",sec={{t="Automated Cleansing",b="Feed toxic and contaminated refuse into the Sparklematic 5200!, and its cycles scour away grime and caustic residue. Once loaded and paid, the machine rattles through its routine. A cheerful ding follows, then a bow-tied present holds whatever remains.",sp=0},{t="Treasure in the Sludge",b="When Gnomeregan fell to the troggs, radiation and industrial mire buried personal effects and scraps of technology. Feed grime-encrusted objects into the machine, and it may recover gemstones, raw ores and other valuables swallowed when the city was vented.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What does the Sparklematic 5200 do?",a="The Sparklematic 5200! cleans objects inside Gnomeregan. Supply a grime-encrusted object and a coin fee, and it scours away sludge, grime and radioactive muck. What remains comes back in a small gift box.",al={"what is sparklematic 5200","how sparklematic works","sparklematic function"},it="purpose"},{q="Where is the Sparklematic 5200 located?",a="The Sparklematic 5200! is inside the corridors of fallen Gnomeregan, near the Clean Zone where survivors and automated decontamination systems once operated.",al={"sparklematic location","where is the cleaning machine","find sparklematic"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the machine wrap items in a bow?",a="Gnomish whimsy gave the Sparklematic 5200! its bow-tied finish. After cleaning fallout and toxic grime from an item, it packages the restored object as a neatly tied present.",al={"why gift box","sparklematic wrapped present","wrapped in bow"}},{q="Can Horde adventurers use the Sparklematic 5200?",a="Yes. The Sparklematic 5200! is automated and pays no heed to faction allegiance. Insert coins and soiled items, and it runs its cycle.",al={"horde sparklematic","can horde clean grime","is sparklematic neutral"},it="side",gp=true},{q="Can I use the Sparklematic multiple times?",a="Yes. After its first operation, the Sparklematic 5200! can clean items again. Bring grime-encrusted objects found throughout the dungeon to put them through another cycle.",al={"is sparklematic repeatable","more sparklematic action","farm grime encrusted objects"},gp=true},{q="What happens after this quest?",a="After the first cleaning, you can use the repeatable More Sparklematic Action cycle to clean any additional grime-encrusted finds you carry.",al={"next quest after sparklematic","what follows sparklematic 5200"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does the Sparklematic 5200 want grime-encrusted objects?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 does not possess personal ambition—it is an automated marvel of gnomish engineering designed to clean and restore salvaged goods. Built before Gnomeregan fell, its programmed function is to wash away thick layers of radioactive muck and debris, packaging whatever remains inside a tidy, wrapped parcel for its user.",al={"why does the sparklematic want this","sparklematic 5200 purpose","why clean grime encrusted objects"},it="motive",add="1a7da75f"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, the Sparklematic recalls home before the fall. Even an industrial scrub unit chimed cheerfully and wrapped its finished work like a birthday present.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can study how the Sparklematic cleans particles automatically and packages items quickly, even amid heavy radiation."},kw={"cleaning","contraption","decontamination","gnomeregan","grime","machine","sparklematic"},rel={"quest:2951","quest:2953","zone:gnomeregan"},m={start="The Sparklematic 5200",faction="Neutral",id=2952},src={"The Sparklematic 5200! (2)"}}
E["quest:2953"] = {t="quest",n="More Sparklematic Action",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, the Sparklematic 5200 still cleans what can be saved. Left behind when the city was evacuated, it scrubs muck and radioactive sludge from curiosities for a small fee in silver.",h="In Gnomeregan, the Sparklematic 5200 still cleans what can be saved.",sec={{t="Automated Restoration",b="Before the trogg invasion and the fallout that followed, Gnomeregan's engineers installed automated devices throughout the city. Toxic waste and hostile automatons now fill its corridors. Yet the Sparklematic 5200 follows its exact programming: it needs three silver coins and an artifact caked in grime to begin.",sp=0},{t="Wonders from the Muck",b="The Sparklematic lurches as it sprays an inserted relic with potent gnomish solvents and scrubs it clean. A cheerful chime marks the end of the cycle, and the machine dispenses a neatly packaged box. Inside is whatever salvage remained beneath corrosive trogg slime and toxic filth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Sparklematic 5200?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 is an automated gnomish cleaning device inside Gnomeregan. It strips caustic sludge, grime, and radioactive residue from recovered objects, leaving salvage that can be identified.",al={"sparklematic 5200","what does the machine do","gnomeregan cleaner"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the machine charge coins?",a="The Sparklematic needs three silver coins to begin a cleaning cycle. No reason for the charge is given.",al={"why pay silver","sparklematic cost"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What kinds of objects can be put inside?",a="The machine cleans grime-encrusted objects, including relics recovered from fallen troggs, corrupted sentries, and irradiated horrors in Gnomeregan's tunnels.",al={"grime-encrusted object","what items can i clean"},it="item"},{q="Is the Sparklematic safe from radiation?",a="Radioactive waste fills Gnomeregan's exterior tunnels, but the Sparklematic 5200 still works. Its specialized gnomish cleaning agents scrub dangerous residue from incoming objects.",al={"sparklematic irradiated","sparklematic contamination"},it="danger"},{q="Can both factions use the Sparklematic 5200?",a="Yes. The Sparklematic 5200 is an automated mechanical installation that accepts payment and grime-encrusted items from visitors of either allegiance.",al={"horde sparklematic","who can use it"},it="allies",gp=true},{q="Who designed the Sparklematic?",a="The Sparklematic's creator is not named. The gnomish cleaning machine still works inside Gnomeregan.",al={"sparklematic creator","who built sparklematic"},it="origin"},{q="Why does the Sparklematic 5200 need to be run?",a="The Sparklematic 5200 is an automated gnomish appliance designed for a single purpose: scrubbing away heavy subterranean muck and industrial buildup from contaminated gear. As a machine, it harbors no grand ambitions or hidden stakes; it simply sits awaiting the proper fee and grime-encrusted objects to activate its cleaning cycles and dispense restored goods.",al={"why run sparklematic","sparklematic motive","why use sparklematic 5200"},it="motive",add="9d072b2b"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you can see your people's mechanical endurance in the Sparklematic, still working amid the toxic ruins of your homeland.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can study the device's sturdy gnomish solvent cycles and coin-activated mechanisms firsthand."},kw={"automation","clean machine","cleaning","gnomeregan","grime-encrusted","sparklematic"},rel={"quest:2951","zone:gnomeregan"},m={start="Sparklematic 5200",faction="Neutral",id=2953},src={"More Sparklematic Action"}}
E["quest:2962"] = {t="quest",n="The Only Cure is More Green Glow",z="gnomeregan",s="In Kharanos, Ozzie Togglevolt seeks a cure for the leper gnomes. He needs a pure sample of fallout from deep inside Gnomeregan.",h="In Kharanos, Ozzie Togglevolt seeks a cure for the leper gnomes.",sec={{t="A Pure Sample",b="Ozzie Togglevolt's first tests outside Gnomeregan gave him no answers. The troggs in Dun Morogh carried too little residue, and what they bore was impure. Now, from his lab in Kharanos, Ozzie seeks a fresh, concentrated sample from deep inside the city. He hopes it will help him find a remedy for the leper gnomes.",sp=0},{t="Straight from the Tap",b="You need to gather potent fallout from inside Gnomeregan. Irradiated horrors, lurkers, and slimes fill the lower depths around the Hall of Gears and Clean Zone. Their unstable ooze must be carried in a heavy leaden phial, and the work is dangerous. The fallout quickly loses its potency, so you need to get it to Ozzie's lab in Kharanos in time.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Ozzie need radioactive fallout?",a="Ozzie Togglevolt seeks a cure for the leper gnomes, whose minds and bodies were ruined by the fallout released during Gnomeregan's fall. He believes a pure sample of the poison may help reverse its effects.",al={"ozzie togglevolt cure","why get green glow","cure for leper gnomes"},it="motive"},{q="Where does the player find the fallout?",a="You can gather fallout from living irradiated horrors, lurkers, and slimes in Gnomeregan's depths, especially around the Hall of Gears and past the Clean Zone.",al={"where is high potency radioactive fallout","fallout location gnomeregan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why were the surface trogg samples rejected?",a="Troggs outside Gnomeregan carried too little contamination, and their samples were impure. They could not give Ozzie reliable material for his research into a cure.",al={"why not troggs","what was wrong with gnogaine"}},{q="Why is the fallout on a time limit?",a="The fallout is unstable and quickly loses potency, even in a leaden phial. It must reach Ozzie's lab in Kharanos before it breaks down.",al={"why does fallout expire","fallout duration"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Who are the leper gnomes Ozzie hopes to help?",a="Leper gnomes were citizens of Gnomeregan, trapped inside when the radiation valves opened to fight the troggs. They survived, but became sickened and deranged, hostile to their former kin.",al={"leper gnomes lore","what are leper gnomes"},it="people"},{q="Who assigns this task?",a="Ozzie Togglevolt is a gnome researcher based in Kharanos in Dun Morogh. He asks you to gather fallout as he works to remedy the harm caused by Gnomeregan's catastrophe.",al={"who gives the quest","ozzie togglevolt location"},it="in_charge"},{q="What is the High Potency Radioactive Fallout used for?",a="Ozzie Togglevolt needs the concentrated fallout to study the intense radiation that engulfed Gnomeregan. His ultimate goal is finding a cure for the leper gnomes, his transformed brethren whose minds and bodies were warped by the disaster. Because earlier surface samples from wandering troggs proved too weak and contaminated to yield actionable scientific results, he requires potent, undiluted radiation straight from the creatures inside the ruined city.",al={"what is radioactive fallout for","high potency fallout use","fallout purpose ozzie"},it="item",add="a4e93100"},{q="What creatures are you hunting inside Gnomeregan?",a="You are sent to harvest samples from the irradiated slimes, lurkers, and horrors festering within Gnomeregan. These wretched oozes and mutated beings formed directly in the wake of the toxic fallout released during the city's fall, absorbing massive concentrations of raw radioactive waste. Because they embody the fallout in its purest, most active state, extracting residue directly from them provides the undiluted potency Ozzie requires for his research.",al={"what are irradiated slimes","who do i kill for fallout","gnomeregan fallout creatures"},it="target",add="089f8395"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you carry the grief of your lost home. Helping Ozzie learn whether the mutations can be undone offers hope of redeeming your fallen kin.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you know radiation calls for sturdy lead shielding and precise instruments. Gnomeregan shows the cost of engineering failure.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can help stabilize Dun Morogh and reclaim Gnomeregan by learning how to face the lethal hazards threatening Ironforge's doorstep."},kw={"gnogaine","gnomeregan","hall of gears","kharanos","leper gnome","ozzie togglevolt","radiation","radioactive fallout"},rel={"quest:2926","quest:2927","npc:ozzie-togglevolt","zone:gnomeregan","topic:leper-gnome","subzone:hall-of-gears","subzone:clean-zone","subzone:kharanos"},m={start="Ozzie Togglevolt",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=2962,ri={"High Potency Radioactive Fallout"}},src={"The Only Cure is More Green Glow"}}
E["subzone:clean-zone"] = {t="subzone",n="Clean Zone",z="gnomeregan",s="Gnomes hold the Clean Zone as a refuge inside ruined Gnomeregan. Beyond the upper Hall of Gears, this fortified enclave stays safe amid the irradiated city. Medics, technicians, and Sparklematic machines support its defenders and salvage work.",h="Gnomes hold the Clean Zone as a refuge inside ruined Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="A Bastion in the Slag",b="The Clean Zone remains untainted while most of Gnomeregan fell to Mekkatorque's disastrous venting of radioactive waste. It lies between the trogg-infested Dormitory below and the contested Hall of Gears above. Gnome defenders, technicians, and field medics hold its barricades day and night. Alliance expeditions regroup here, tend wounds, and maintain their machinery.",sp=0},{t="The Sparklematic 5200",b="The Clean Zone also supports salvage from Gnomeregan's ruined capital. Gnomish engineers installed Sparklematic 5200 units to scrub and wash grime-encrusted relics brought up from the city's radioactive depths. Technicians and merchants such as Tink Sprocketwhistle process reclaimed gears and baubles, outfit adventurers, and study the toxic fallout in the deep tunnels.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why isn't this area irradiated like the rest of Gnomeregan?",a="Gnomes in the Clean Zone remain unaffected by the radiation that devastated Gnomeregan. No account explains exactly why this small area escaped contamination.",al={"why clean zone not irradiated","why safe here","clean zone radiation"},it="name"},{q="What do the Sparklematic 5200 machines do?",a="Sparklematic 5200s are gnomish machines that launder and decontaminate objects. Adventurers can put grime-encrusted objects taken from troggs and leper gnomes inside. The machines wash away radioactive grime and reveal useful ores, gems, coins, or engineering oddities.",al={"sparklematic 5200","what are sparklematics","clean grime"},gp=true},{q="Who controls and defends the Clean Zone?",a="Uncorrupted gnomish guards, field medics, and technicians hold the Clean Zone's perimeter. They fight troggs advancing from the Dormitory and leper gnomes descending from the upper levels to keep the staging post secure.",al={"who is in clean zone","clean zone guards","who holds clean zone"},it="residents"},{q="Can players safely rest or repair here?",a="Yes. The Clean Zone is a field camp inside Gnomeregan, with engineering supplies, repairs from Tink Sprocketwhistle, and a working mailbox for adventurers behind the front lines.",al={"repairs clean zone","can you rest in clean zone","mailbox in gnomeregan"},gp=true},{q="What is the Clean Zone?",a="The Clean Zone is a fortified sanctuary located deep within Gnomeregan, lying just beyond the upper level of the Hall of Gears. It stands as the last remaining stronghold inside the fallen capital where uncorrupted gnomes maintain a foothold free from the lethal fallout.",al={"what is clean zone","clean zone overview","about clean zone"},it="place",add="dc9c4202"},{q="What happened to the Clean Zone during the fall of Gnomeregan?",a="When High Tinker Mekkatorque opened the radiation valves to purge the invading troggs, toxic fallout devastated the city and mutated many gnomes into leper gnomes. Unaffected gnomes hold this small refuge and defend it against surrounding invaders.",al={"clean zone history","what happened at clean zone","history of clean zone"},it="history",add="fa9b1319"},{q="Is the Clean Zone dangerous?",a="The interior of the Clean Zone itself is safe and well defended by elite gnome guards and medics. However, the areas directly flanking it are perilous: hostile troggs infest the dormitory below and swarm the upper levels of the Hall of Gears right outside its perimeter.",al={"is clean zone dangerous","threats in clean zone","clean zone danger"},it="danger",add="844f3e3b"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you see the Clean Zone as a grim reminder of your home's fall and a beacon of hope that Gnomeregan's technology can still be reclaimed from the troggs.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can use the working Sparklematic 5200 units here to scour irradiated junk for rare schematics and mechanical parts. Merchant Tink Sprocketwhistle is here too."},kw={"clean zone","dormitory","gnomeregan","hall of gears","radiation","sparklematic 5200","tink sprocketwhistle","troggs"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:hall-of-gears","subzone:dormitory","topic:gnome","topic:trogg"},src={"Clean Zone"}}
E["subzone:clockwerk-run"] = {t="subzone",n="Clockwerk Run",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, toxic fumes and irradiated troggs choke Clockwerk Run between the Train Depot and the Hall of Gears.",h="In Gnomeregan, toxic fumes and irradiated troggs choke Clockwerk Run between the Train Depot and the Hall of...",sec={{t="A Ruined Threshold",b="Clockwerk Run carries you from the outer Train Depot into Gnomeregan. Once, gnomish traffic and supplies passed through this corridor. Then High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered radioactive waste vented to stop the trogg invasion. The waste turned the passage into a deadly trap.\n\nThe blast and the fighting that followed brought parts of the hallway down. Toxic fumes and irradiated troggs now block the way to the upper Hall of Gears.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the Clockwerk Run lead?",a="Clockwerk Run connects the Train Depot outside the deep vaults to the upper Hall of Gears inside Gnomeregan.",al={"clockwerk run location","where does this hallway go","clockwerk run entrance"},it="place"},{q="Why are there so many troggs here?",a="Troggs surged through Gnomeregan's lower passages during the invasion. In Clockwerk Run, vented radioactive waste made them violent and irradiated, and they attack anyone entering the city.",al={"why troggs","clockwerk run enemies"},it="threat"},{q="Why is the corridor partially caved in?",a="Fighting during Gnomeregan's fall and the release of toxic counter-measures badly damaged the perimeter. Parts of the corridor collapsed.",al={"clockwerk run collapsed","why is it broken"},it="ruin"},{q="What is the Clockwerk Run?",a="The Clockwerk Run is the grand entrance corridor leading directly into the depths of Gnomeregan. Stretching from the upper Train Depot down toward the Hall of Gears, it was once a bustling transit artery connecting the gnome capital's outer transit systems to its industrial heart. Today, it stands as a broken, hazardous gateway into the fallen city.",al={"what is clockwerk run","clockwerk run overview","what is this area"},it="place",add="8c8c10db"},{q="What happened to the Clockwerk Run?",a="When troggs surged from the deep caverns to overrun Gnomeregan, the gnomes unleashed toxic radioactive gas in a desperate attempt to eradicate the invaders. The plan failed catastrophically: the gnomes were forced to flee or perished, the corridor partially collapsed under the chaos, and irradiated troggs claimed the passageway for themselves.",al={"clockwerk run history","what happened at clockwerk run","fall of clockwerk run"},it="history",add="556e3735"},{q="Who controls the Clockwerk Run now?",a="No civilized authority controls the run anymore. The corridor is overrun entirely by savage troggs who were mutated by the toxic fallout unleashed during the fall of Gnomeregan. They attack any outsiders who dare tread through the ruined passage.",al={"who lives in clockwerk run","who controls clockwerk run","who runs clockwerk run"},it="residents",add="c5bdf1c1"},{q="Is the Clockwerk Run dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally perilous. The passageway is crawling with hostile, irradiated troggs driven mad by lingering fallout, while sections of the ceiling and walls have suffered structural collapse. Anyone venturing down this corridor must be prepared to fight through swarms of mutated beasts amid unstable ruins.",al={"is clockwerk run dangerous","clockwerk run dangers","clockwerk run threats"},it="danger",add="aa198084"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, passing through Clockwerk Run brings the fall of your capital close. The desperate attempt to cleanse the city changed the invaders instead of destroying them.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, the ruined machinery and collapsed structures along Clockwerk Run show what explosive force and radiation can do to gnomish mechanisms."},kw={"clockwerk run","gnomeregan","hall of gears","irradiated troggs","train depot","troggs"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:hall-of-gears","subzone:train-depot","topic:trogg","topic:gnome"},src={"Clockwerk Run"}}
E["subzone:dormitory"] = {t="subzone",n="Dormitory",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, troggs now overrun the Dormitory, and radiation chokes its halls. Gnomes once made their homes here, but the creatures that drove them out now hold the fallen city's residential quarters.",h="In Gnomeregan, troggs now overrun the Dormitory, and radiation chokes its halls.",sec={{t="A Home Overrun",b="Beyond the Clean Zone's decontamination chambers, the Dormitory once housed Gnomeregan's inventors, laborers, and families. When High Tinker Mekkatorque opened the emergency radiation vents to fight the invading troggs, this crowded part of the city became a trap. No gnomish life remains in its communal halls or living quarters. Mutated troggs thrive in the radioactive air. To reach the lower Hall of Gears, travelers must fight through this reminder of the catastrophe.",sp=0},{t="Punchograph Terminals",b="Though the living quarters are abandoned, Gnomeregan's administrative machines still work. Matrix Punchograph 3005-B terminals process security punch cards. The cards open higher-security data terminals deeper in the city, where important records remain from the gnomes' flight.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was the Dormitory used for before the fall?",a="The Dormitory housed Gnomeregan's inventors, workers, and families. Near the industrial and civic sectors, residents could reach their workstations and sleeping bunks before toxic radiation flooded the lower corridors.",al={"what is dormitory","dormitory purpose","who lived here"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is the Dormitory infested with troggs?",a="When troggs broke into the city from below, High Tinker Mekkatorque flooded it with toxic gas to kill them. Radiation instead mutated the survivors, leaving them more vicious and wholly resistant to the irradiated residential blocks.",al={"why troggs here","trogg infestation dormitory","irradiated troggs"},it="threat"},{q="Where does the Dormitory lead?",a="The Dormitory lies beyond the Clean Zone's sanitized airlocks and connects the upper levels to the lower Hall of Gears. Anyone going deeper into Gnomeregan must pass through it.",al={"dormitory exits","where to go from dormitory","dormitory connections"},gp=true},{q="What are the Matrix Punchograph machines found here?",a="Matrix Punchograph 3005-B terminals process security punch cards. The encoded cards open higher-security terminals and help recover important data left behind in Gnomeregan.",al={"punchograph","matrix punchograph 3005-B","punch cards"},it="item"},{q="What is the Dormitory?",a="The Dormitory is a residential subzone inside Gnomeregan, situated just past the Clean Zone and the upper level of the Hall of Gears. Once a bustling, closely packed quarter where many of the city's gnome citizens lived and rested, it now stands derelict, connecting downward into the Hall of Gears' lower tier.",al={"what is dormitory","dormitory gnomeregan","about dormitory"},it="place",add="a2c6e6cc"},{q="What happened to the Dormitory?",a="When the trogg invasion overwhelmed Gnomeregan and toxic radiation flooded the lower corridors, the Dormitory was entirely lost. Its resident gnomes were either slain, forced to flee to Ironforge, or mutated by fallout, leaving their personal quarters behind to rot as subterranean horrors took over.",al={"what happened at dormitory","dormitory fall","dormitory history"},it="history",add="47f03a0e"},{q="Why was the Dormitory abandoned?",a="The Dormitory was abandoned during the catastrophic fall of the city. As toxic radiation permeated the sector to halt the subterranean trogg outbreak, the living quarters became unlivable for normal gnomes, turning the once-cozy bunkhouses into a poisoned ruin.",al={"why is dormitory ruined","dormitory abandoned","why did gnomes leave dormitory"},it="ruin",add="9c6fea46"},{q="Who lives in the Dormitory now?",a="No civilized citizens remain. The quarters have been thoroughly overrun by irradiated troggs, vicious subterranean brutes warped by the fallout that choked Gnomeregan during its final hours.",al={"who controls dormitory","dormitory inhabitants","who lives in dormitory"},it="residents",add="410e0de9"},{q="Is the Dormitory dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. Anyone passing beyond the safety of the nearby Clean Zone steps right into the path of irradiated troggs, who swarm the narrow halls and attack intruders on sight amidst lingering toxic contamination.",al={"dormitory danger","is dormitory safe","threats in dormitory"},it="danger",add="33cb3e50"},{q="Why is this area called the Dormitory?",a="It bears the literal name of its original function: the collective sleeping and living quarters for a vast portion of Gnomeregan's working population before the fall.",al={"why called dormitory","dormitory name meaning","dormitory origin"},it="name",add="68138d13"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, the Dormitory was once home. Now irradiated rubble fills its halls, overrun by the brutes who drove your people out.",["profession:Engineering"]="Even amid a failure of bio-containment, automated Matrix Punchograph 3005-B terminals still process algorithmic security punch cards without fail."},kw={"clean zone","dormitory","gnomeregan","hall of gears","punchograph","trogg"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:clean-zone","subzone:hall-of-gears","topic:gnome","topic:trogg"},src={"Dormitory"}}
E["subzone:engineering-labs"] = {t="subzone",n="Engineering Labs",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, the Engineering Labs lie in ruin across tiers linked to the Workshop Entrance and Launch Bay. Once a center of gnome invention, they fell in the city's radioactive catastrophe. Crazed leper gnomes and rogue machines now fill the chambers.",h="In Gnomeregan, the Engineering Labs lie in ruin across tiers linked to the Workshop Entrance and Launch Bay.",sec={{t="A Fallen Center of Innovation",b="The Engineering Labs once held Gnomeregan's work in invention. A central mechanical structure rises through two tiers, joined by a cargo lift. At the city's height, tinkerers made schematics and refined clockwork devices here. Radiation drove the remaining researchers mad. Now deranged leper gnomes guard the malfunctioning machinery beside rogue constructs.",sp=0},{t="Crucial Junction",b="The Engineering Labs connect routes through Gnomeregan's lower reaches. Passages lead toward the Launch Bay, Tinkers' Court and the Workshop Entrance back door. On the lower floor, Matrix Punchograph 3005-D terminals process coded punch cards carried by gnome engineers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What were the Engineering Labs originally used for?",a="Before Gnomeregan fell, engineers researched, assembled and tested complex contraptions and automated devices in the Engineering Labs. Technicians used the vast two-level chamber to blueprint new technology.",al={"purpose of engineering labs","what was made here","engineering labs lore"},it="purpose"},{q="What threats roam the Engineering Labs now?",a="Irradiated leper gnomes and haywire mechanical automatons roam both tiers. Gas released during the city's fall drove the lingering residents mad, and they attack any non-irradiated intruders on sight.",al={"who is inside","enemies in engineering labs","monsters here"},it="threat"},{q="What are the Matrix Punchograph 3005-D machines?",a="Matrix Punchograph 3005-D machines are automated data terminals on the Engineering Labs' lower level. Engineers and adventurers use them to punch encoded data cards, advance their security clearance and decipher technical archives preserved within the city.",al={"punchograph d","matrix punchograph 3005-d","yellow card machine"},it="item"},{q="How does this area connect to the rest of Gnomeregan?",a="The upper level connects to the Workshop Entrance back door and passages toward the Launch Bay. The lower level leads to main corridors linking the Launch Bay and Tinkers' Court.",al={"where does this lead","engineering labs exits","routes to engineering labs"},gp=true},{q="What is the Engineering Labs?",a="The Engineering Labs form a multi-tiered research sector deep within the ruined techno-city of Gnomeregan. Composed of an upper circuit and a lower floor linked by an open lift platform, it once housed high-level technological experiments, automated systems, and diagnostic machinery such as the Matrix Punchograph 3005-D units.",al={"what are the engineering labs","engineering labs gnomeregan","about engineering labs"},it="place",add="36276ef1"},{q="What happened to the Engineering Labs?",a="When the troggs breached Gnomeregan, High Tinker Mekkatorque authorized the release of toxic radiation to eradicate the invaders. Instead of saving the city, the fallout saturated sectors like the Engineering Labs. The gnomes working within were either killed or horribly twisted into irradiated leper gnomes, while their mechanical contraptions ran wild.",al={"engineering labs history","what happened here","fall of engineering labs"},it="history",add="a7c381fe"},{q="Who controls the Engineering Labs now?",a="No sane gnome remains in charge here. The laboratories are infested with deranged leper gnomes and haywire mechanical constructs that tirelessly patrol both levels, including the hulking Crowd Pummeler 9-60 on the upper level's southern side.",al={"who lives in engineering labs","engineering labs residents","who runs the engineering labs"},it="residents",add="526db480"},{q="Why are the Engineering Labs ruined and abandoned?",a="The labs were abandoned during the tragic fall of Gnomeregan, when radioactive venting flooded the halls to combat the trogg invasion. The catastrophic exposure rendered the entire facility uninhabitable to uncorrupted gnomes, leaving valuable equipment, blueprints, and terminals at the mercy of mad survivors and rogue automatons.",al={"why are engineering labs ruined","why was engineering labs abandoned","fall of the labs"},it="ruin",add="2ced7fd6"},{q="Is it dangerous to explore the Engineering Labs?",a="The labs are exceedingly hazardous. Beyond the lingering taint of radiation throughout Gnomeregan, you must contend with aggressive leper gnomes, malfunctioning machinery, and hostile constructs such as the Crowd Pummeler 9-60 patrolling the upper circuit.",al={"are engineering labs dangerous","engineering labs hazards","danger in engineering labs"},it="danger",add="620f0877"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="In the Engineering Labs, functional punchograph terminals and discarded schematics reveal the height of gnomish automation before the city's fall.",["race:Gnome"]="As an exiled gnome, you see a tragic ruin. These laboratories once held the heart of your people's technological triumphs. Now irradiated ruins are overrun by your corrupted kin."},kw={"engineering labs","gnomeregan","launch bay","leper gnome","punchograph","tinkers court","workshop entrance"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:workshop-entrance","subzone:launch-bay","subzone:tinkers-court","topic:leper-gnome","topic:gnome"},src={"Engineering Labs"}}
E["subzone:hall-of-gears"] = {t="subzone",n="Hall of Gears",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan, the Hall of Gears lies in ruin beyond the Clockwerk Run. Toxic sludge fills its lower floor, where oozes and irradiated troggs roam.",h="In Gnomeregan, the Hall of Gears lies in ruin beyond the Clockwerk Run.",sec={{t="A Fractured Machine",b="Beyond the Clockwerk Run, the Hall of Gears lies deep within Gnomeregan’s ruined machinery halls. Its two levels show how completely the gnome capital has fallen. Irradiated troggs claw through collapsed access shafts and prowl the upper catwalks. Below, radioactive pools cover the floor. Corrosive slimes and living poison elementals thrive in the toxic runoff.",sp=0},{t="Pathways through the Waste",b="The Hall of Gears links parts of Gnomeregan’s operational quarters. From the upper walkways, paths lead to contaminated dead ends, the Clean Zone, and the Dormitory. Below, winding maintenance passages lead toward the Launch Bay. Horrors left by Mekgineer Thermaplugg’s venting scheme still make both levels dangerous.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Hall of Gears located?",a="The Hall of Gears lies deep inside Gnomeregan, just beyond the Clockwerk Run. Paths from the chamber lead toward the Clean Zone, the Dormitory, and the Launch Bay.",al={"hall of gears location","where is hall of gears","how to get to hall of gears"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is the lower level full of radioactive sludge?",a="When High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered radioactive gas vented to repel the trogg invasion, contaminated runoff collected in the city’s low machinery halls. The Hall of Gears’ lower floor became a toxic wasteland.",al={"why is it green","radioactive waste hall of gears","what is the sludge"},it="ruin"},{q="What creatures inhabit this chamber?",a="Irradiated troggs pour through breach tunnels onto the upper level. Below, radioactive fallout slimes, oozes, and volatile poison elementals formed from the industrial runoff.",al={"hall of gears enemies","what lives in hall of gears","hall of gears mobs"},it="residents"},{q="Where do the exits lead from here?",a="The upper walkways lead southwest toward the Clean Zone and the Dormitory, and southeast to a dead-end maintenance corridor. A winding passage west from the lower floor leads to the Launch Bay.",al={"hall of gears exits","where to go from hall of gears"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Hall of Gears?",a="The Hall of Gears is a massive, multi-tiered chamber within the subterranean city of Gnomeregan, situated just beyond the Clockwerk Run. Like much of the technological wonder that was the gnomish capital, it was once a hub of bustling industry and intricate machinery. Today, it stands as a hazardous corridor divided between irradiated upper catwalks and toxic, sludge-covered depths.",al={"hall of gears overview","what is this place","hall of gears gnomeregan"},it="place",add="d9a40d55"},{q="What happened to the Hall of Gears?",a="When the barbaric troggs breached the city, high tinkers attempted to purge the invaders by flooding the halls with radioactive fallout. Instead of driving the troggs out, the toxic gas mutated them and contaminated the entire sector. The gnomes were forced to evacuate, leaving the Hall of Gears abandoned to irradiated monsters and creeping toxic waste.",al={"hall of gears history","what happened here","gnomeregan disaster hall of gears"},it="history",add="3f6f0027"},{q="Is the Hall of Gears dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The upper tier crawls with feral, irradiated troggs hostile to any intruders. Below, the floor is drowned in pooling radioactive fallout, inhabited by acidic oozes and volatile poison elementals. Traversing the chamber requires avoiding toxic pools and contending with twisted abominations spawned by the city's ruin.",al={"is hall of gears dangerous","hall of gears threats","how dangerous is hall of gears"},it="danger",add="ad0af20b"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you see the great cogs and catwalks submerged in irradiated sludge. They recall the desperate decision that poisoned your city and drove your people into exile.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see the scale of pre-fall gnomish gearing and elevated platforms. Radioactive fallout has heavily corroded them."},kw={"clean zone","clockwerk run","dormitory","gnomeregan","hall of gears","launch bay","radioactive","troggs"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:clockwerk-run","subzone:clean-zone","subzone:dormitory","subzone:launch-bay","npc:sicco-thermaplugg","topic:trogg"},src={"Hall of Gears"}}
E["subzone:launch-bay"] = {t="subzone",n="Launch Bay",z="gnomeregan",s="Hostile leper gnomes and corrupted machines hold Launch Bay beyond the Hall of Gears. Once Gnomeregan’s airfield for flying machines and bombers, this hangar lies deep beneath the city.",h="Hostile leper gnomes and corrupted machines hold Launch Bay beyond the Hall of Gears.",sec={{t="A Grounded Airfield",b="Two tiers once held Gnomeregan’s aerial fleet. Ramps from the upper walkway lead to a central platform, where flying machines and heavy bombers remain parked. They were left behind before the city was evacuated.\n\nCrazed leper gnomes now roam the flight decks. They maintain and guard the idle war machines where skilled pilots once served.",sp=0},{t="Crossroads of the Deep City",b="Launch Bay joins several parts of the complex. Ramps from its southeastern corridor descend into the Engineering Labs.\n\nOn the lower deck, invading Dark Iron dwarves choke the southern passage. That tunnel offers a perilous route toward Tinkers' Court, deep in the city.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Launch Bay used for?",a="Launch Bay was built as an underground airfield and hangar for gnomish flying machines and bombers. Leper gnomes dwelling in the ruins have now taken over the neglected space.",al={"gnomeregan hangar","what is launch bay","launch bay purpose"},it="purpose"},{q="Who controls the Launch Bay now?",a="Leper gnomes and aggressive mechanical contraptions occupy Launch Bay’s upper and lower levels. Hostile Dark Iron dwarves have also carved out a foothold near the southern exits.",al={"who is in launch bay","launch bay enemies","who lives here"},it="in_charge"},{q="Where does the Launch Bay lead?",a="The upper eastern tunnel leads back to the Hall of Gears. Southeastern ramps descend to the Engineering Labs, while a southern tunnel on the lower deck leads deeper into Gnomeregan toward Tinkers' Court.",al={"launch bay exits","how to leave launch bay","launch bay directions"}},{q="Are the flying machines here operational?",a="Several gnomish flying machines and bombers remain parked on the central platforms. They sit idle and untended amid the chaos of the city’s fall.",al={"can i fly the planes","flying machines gnomeregan","hangar planes"}},{q="What is the Launch Bay?",a="The Launch Bay, also known as the Hangar, is a vast multi-tiered facility within the subterranean city of Gnomeregan. Accessible via tunnels connecting from the Hall of Gears, it spans both an upper and lower level designed to store, maintain, and dispatch gnomish flying machines and aerial bombers.",al={"what is launch bay","gnomeregan launch bay","hangar gnomeregan"},it="place",add="7077c2fc"},{q="What happened to the Launch Bay?",a="When the trogg invasion struck Gnomeregan and High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered the venting of radioactive waste, the entire city succumbed to catastrophe. The Launch Bay fell along with the rest of the capital, leaving its flying machines stranded on their pads as the gnomish technicians succumbed to radiation poisoning and insanity.",al={"launch bay history","what happened at the launch bay","why is the launch bay abandoned"},it="history",add="618f410c"},{q="Is the Launch Bay dangerous?",a="Yes, it is extremely dangerous. The bays are swarming with hostile, irradiated leper gnomes and volatile mechanical contraptions. Moreover, the lower exits connect toward tunnels infested with Dark Iron dwarf infiltrators who have pushed into the fallen city to claim its wonders for themselves.",al={"is launch bay dangerous","launch bay dangers","launch bay threats"},it="danger",add="cbaccda1"},{q="Why is it called the Launch Bay?",a="It earned its name as the primary staging ground and hangar for Gnomeregan's air fleet. From its platforms, gnomish pilots once scrambled their flying machines and experimental bombers into the sky through subterranean exhaust and launch chutes.",al={"why is it called launch bay","launch bay name origin","launch bay name meaning"},it="name",add="c8b4c6a3"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, seeing flying machines and bombers abandoned and overrun by irradiated leper kin is a bitter reminder of your city’s tragic loss.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can see the hangar’s gnomish aeronautics and vehicle chassis up close, though hostile contraptions guard the area."},kw={"bomber","dark iron","engineering labs","flying machine","gnomeregan","hangar","launch bay","leper gnome"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:hall-of-gears","subzone:engineering-labs","subzone:tinkers-court","topic:leper-gnome","topic:gnome"},src={"Launch Bay"}}
E["subzone:loading-room"] = {t="subzone",n="Loading Room",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan's depths, the Loading Room lies amid danger. It once staged cargo for the city's transit networks. Now radioactive fallout and rogue machinery threaten all who enter.",h="In Gnomeregan's depths, the Loading Room lies amid danger.",sec={{t="Industrial Depot Under Siege",b="Cargo once passed through the Loading Room on its way across Gnomeregan's underground transit network. Goods gathered in its staging bay before the trains carried them through the tinker capital.\n\nNow ruin has overtaken the chamber. Radioactive fallout, invading troggs, and failing machinery make it perilous. Techbot, a rogue mechanized construct, guards the vicinity. Gnome survivors and Alliance reclaimers who try to secure the perimeter must face that danger.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Loading Room used for?",a="The Loading Room once staged cargo for Gnomeregan's internal transport and train facilities. Since the city fell, hazards have overrun this lost sector.",al={"loading room purpose","what is loading room","what was loading room"},it="purpose"},{q="What threats can be found in the Loading Room?",a="Techbot, a rogue mechanical defense construct, prowls the Loading Room. Radioactive contamination and erratic machinery threaten anyone in this part of the city.",al={"who is in loading room","loading room bosses","techbot location"},it="threat"},{q="Is the Loading Room safe to explore?",a="No. The Loading Room lies in contested ground among Gnomeregan's ruins. Alliance strike teams entering the complex face hostile constructs and toxic conditions.",al={"is it safe","can alliance go here"},it="danger"},{q="What is the Loading Room?",a="The Loading Room is an industrial chamber within the fallen technological marvel of Gnomeregan. Situated deep inside the city's complex infrastructure, it previously served mechanical transit and cargo functions before the city was overtaken by troggs and irradiated. In our current era, it lies directly in the path of those navigating the hazards of the irradiated subterranean metropolis.",al={"what is loading room","gnomeregan loading room","about loading room"},it="place",add="3f72b894"},{q="What happened to the Loading Room?",a="Like the rest of Gnomeregan, the Loading Room fell during the trogg invasion and the subsequent release of the catastrophic radioactive fallout. When High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and his advisors vented radioactive gases to halt the subterranean beasts, the toxic radiation spread uncontrollably, mutating defenders and leaving once-bustling industrial sectors like this room abandoned or overrun by rogue constructs like Techbot.",al={"loading room history","what happened in loading room","why fell loading room"},it="history",add="a3501e82"},{q="Why is the Loading Room ruined?",a="The chamber was abandoned along with the rest of the lower city when the catastrophic radioactive venting failed to eradicate the trogg invaders. Instead of saving the city, the radiation poisoned the population, warped the surviving gnomes into lepers, and left automated defense systems and mechanized caretakers running berserk without oversight.",al={"why is loading room ruined","loading room abandoned","why is it destroyed"},it="ruin",add="6c9ce16b"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="For gnomish reclaimers, the Loading Room recalls how ordinary city works were abandoned during the trogg invasion and toxic catastrophe.",["profession:Engineering"]="Techbot and the remaining mechanical assemblies in the Loading Room show engineers the danger of automated defenses left without maintenance."},kw={"dun morogh","gnomeregan","loading room","techbot","tinkertown","train depot"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:train-depot","subzone:dormitory"},src={"Loading Room"}}
E["subzone:tinkers-court"] = {t="subzone",n="Tinkers' Court",z="gnomeregan",s="In Gnomeregan's heart, Tinkers' Court once brought the city's leaders together. Now Mekgineer Thermaplugg holds the chamber.",h="In Gnomeregan's heart, Tinkers' Court once brought the city's leaders together.",sec={{t="Seat of the Gnomish Council",b="Before disaster drove the gnomes from Gnomeregan, their leaders gathered in Tinkers' Court. High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque met there with advisors and master inventors, among them Tinkmaster Overspark. They debated new technology, governed civic matters, and guided gnomish society. Beyond the Engineering Labs and the Launch Bay, the chamber stood at the heart of gnomish government and invention.",sp=0},{t="Thermaplugg's Throneroom",b="After radiation drove the gnomes into exile, Mekgineer Thermaplugg claimed Tinkers' Court. He calls himself King of Gnomeregan and sits among twisted contraptions, loyal leper gnomes, and bomb dispensers. From the chamber, he directs his remaining forces. Anyone seeking to end his rule must face this final and dangerous threshold.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was the Tinkers' Court used for originally?",a="Tinkers' Court was the meeting hall and civic chamber of Gnomeregan's High Tinker and ruling council. Gelbin Mekkatorque and advisors such as Tinkmaster Overspark gathered there to govern and discuss new inventions.",al={"tinkers court history","what is tinkers court","original purpose of court"},it="purpose"},{q="Who controls Tinkers' Court now?",a="Mekgineer Thermaplugg controls Tinkers' Court. He calls himself King of Gnomeregan and holds the chamber with defensive machinery and irradiated minions.",al={"who is in tinkers court","boss in tinkers court","thermaplugg room"},it="residents"},{q="Where is the court located within Gnomeregan?",a="Tinkers' Court lies deep within Gnomeregan, beyond the dark tunnels and lower levels connected to the Launch Bay and Engineering Labs.",al={"where is tinkers court","how to get to tinkers court","find tinkers court"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is reaching Tinkers' Court so important for the Alliance?",a="Mekgineer Thermaplugg directs his irradiated minions from Tinkers' Court. Reaching him is the first step toward freeing Gnomeregan from his rule.",al={"why go to tinkers court","kill thermaplugg why","importance of tinkers court"},it="motive"},{q="What is the Tinkers' Court?",a="Tinkers' Court is the deepest administrative heart of Gnomeregan. In peaceful days, it served as the grand chamber where the elected High Tinker and the ruling council convened to guide the gnomish people, debate engineering marvels, and oversee civic life. Now, it stands as a fortified inner sanctum claimed by traitors.",al={"what is tinkers court","tinkers court gnomeregan","about tinkers court"},it="place",add="d2a5bbc9"},{q="What happened to the Tinkers' Court during the fall of Gnomeregan?",a="When the trogg invasion struck, High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and his advisors governed from this hall. Following Mekgineer Thermaplugg's disastrous advice to vent radiation throughout the city to purge the beasts, the court was overwhelmed by toxic fallout. Mekkatorque and the survivors were forced to flee, leaving the chamber in the hands of the mad betrayer.",al={"what happened at tinkers court","tinkers court history","fall of tinkers court"},it="history",add="66d32e28"},{q="Why was the Tinkers' Court abandoned and ruined?",a="The court was abandoned during the cataclysmic irradiation of Gnomeregan. The deadly radioactive vapors that blanketed the lower levels made normal gnomish life impossible, mutating those left behind into crazed leper gnomes and turning the grand seat of government into a polluted, mechanical fortress.",al={"why is tinkers court ruined","tinkers court abandoned","why ruined"},it="ruin",add="fddc0bd4"},{q="How dangerous is the Tinkers' Court?",a="It is the most heavily fortified and perilous chamber in the entire ruined city. Mekgineer Thermaplugg has surrounded himself with lethal robotic guardians, walking mechanostriders, and fanatical leper gnome servants. Entering means braving crushing machinery, toxic exposure, and the mad tinker's deadliest combat inventions.",al={"is tinkers court dangerous","tinkers court threats","how dangerous is tinkers court"},it="danger",add="19b28a1e"},{q="Why is it named the Tinkers' Court?",a="Gnomish society is led not by hereditary monarchs, but by elected visionary inventors known as High Tinkers, who govern alongside an assembly of master crafters and scholars. The chamber took its name from this ruling body, serving as the literal court where tinkers gathered to lead their people.",al={"why called tinkers court","tinkers court name meaning","why the name tinkers court"},it="name",add="a5ad6256"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, Tinkers' Court recalls betrayal. Gnomish leaders once gathered here, before Mekgineer Thermaplugg seized the chamber amid irradiated ruin.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, Tinkers' Court shows engineering turned deadly, with bomb delivery systems and the siege suit Thermaplugg operates."},kw={"council","gnomeregan","high tinker","mekkatorque","overspark","thermaplugg","tinkers court"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","npc:gelbin-mekkatorque","quest:2923","subzone:engineering-labs","subzone:launch-bay"},src={"Tinkers' Court"}}
E["subzone:train-depot"] = {t="subzone",n="Train Depot",z="gnomeregan",s="Beneath Gnomeregan's entrance in Dun Morogh, the Train Depot lies overrun by leper gnomes and troggs. Once, its rails carried gnomes through the city. Now the depot is in ruin.",h="Beneath Gnomeregan's entrance in Dun Morogh, the Train Depot lies overrun by leper gnomes and troggs.",sec={{t="A Ruined Transit Hub",b="Beneath the grand elevator from Dun Morogh, the Train Depot's platforms and tracks lie in ruin. Once, rail lines carried gnomes through Gnomeregan. Radiation swept through the city and changed the workers who remained into crazed leper gnomes. Troggs from below have overrun the rails. You must cross the depot to reach deeper parts of the city, including Clockwerk Run, the Loading Room, and the inner engineering facilities.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Train Depot located?",a="The Train Depot lies beneath the surface entrance elevator in Dun Morogh, before Gnomeregan's inner parts.",al={"train depot location","how to get to train depot","train depot entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What creatures inhabit the Train Depot now?",a="Feral troggs from deep underground and leper gnomes driven mad by the radioactive disaster overrun the depot.",al={"train depot enemies","mobs in train depot","who is in train depot"},it="threat"},{q="Where do the paths from the Train Depot lead?",a="Passages lead west into Clockwerk Run and toward the Loading Room. A northern workshop's back door leads down to the upper Engineering Labs.",al={"train depot exits","where does train depot go","train depot connections"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Who is hiding in the Train Depot?",a="Namdo Bizzfizzle, an engineering supplier, survives beneath the north side of the main platform on the depot's lower level.",al={"namdo bizzfizzle","train depot npc","train depot vendor"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Train Depot?",a="The Train Depot is an expansive transit sector situated just beneath the entry elevators of Gnomeregan. Before the fall of the city, it served as a bustling transportation hub connecting the upper reaches to the deeper workshops and central facilities.",al={"what is train depot","train depot gnomeregan","about train depot"},it="place",add="08edd791"},{q="What happened to the Train Depot?",a="When the trogg invasion and the subsequent irradiation overwhelmed Gnomeregan, the city's rail and transit systems were completely disrupted. The depot was quickly abandoned by sane gnomes, left to rot alongside the rest of the ruined subterranean metropolis.",al={"train depot history","what happened here train depot","fall of train depot"},it="history",add="34ec9e38"},{q="Why is the Train Depot ruined?",a="The catastrophic release of radioactive fallout throughout Gnomeregan wiped out normal operations. The infrastructure collapsed as surviving workers turned into mindless leper gnomes or fled, leaving the depot's machinery and corridors neglected and overgrown with hostile threats.",al={"why is train depot abandoned","why is train depot destroyed","train depot ruined"},it="ruin",add="b2726984"},{q="How dangerous is the Train Depot?",a="The area is exceptionally dangerous for unprepared travelers. Savage subterranean troggs and irradiated, hostile leper gnomes prowl the platforms and corridors, attacking anyone who descends from Dun Morogh without hesitation.",al={"is train depot dangerous","train depot threats","danger in train depot"},it="danger",add="ab6b6be9"},{q="Why is it called the Train Depot?",a="It earned its name from its original design as a central rail station and loading terminal for the complex mechanical train networks that once hauled cargo and passengers throughout Gnomeregan.",al={"why train depot","train depot name meaning","is there a train here"},it="name",add="9f84ab0b"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As an exiled gnome, you see the abandoned depot as a reminder of the advanced rail systems that once joined your subterranean city.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can search the depot's lower platforms for rare schematics. Gnome peddlers such as Namdo Bizzfizzle still trade among the wreckage."},kw={"clockwerk run","dun morogh","gnomeregan","leper gnome","loading room","namdo bizzfizzle","train depot","trogg"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","zone:dunmorogh","subzone:clockwerk-run","subzone:loading-room","subzone:engineering-labs","topic:leper-gnome","topic:trogg","topic:gnome"},src={"Train Depot"}}
E["subzone:workshop-entrance"] = {t="subzone",n="Workshop Entrance",z="gnomeregan",s="Past the Train Depot, Workshop Entrance offers another way into Gnomeregan. The passage skirts the front gates and reaches the Engineering Labs in the irradiated city.",h="Past the Train Depot, Workshop Entrance offers another way into Gnomeregan.",sec={{t="The Backdoor to the City",b="Past the Train Depot, Workshop Entrance crosses the cavernous workshop floor toward Gnomeregan’s industrial heart. The opening to the Loading Room lies on one side. The passage runs straight to the Engineering Labs, away from the fortified gates near the surface. There, leper gnomes and troggs contest the way. Those seeking to reclaim the underground capital can use this side door to bypass the first perimeter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Workshop Entrance located?",a="Workshop Entrance lies across the workshop floor, past the Train Depot in Gnomeregan’s outer corridors. The opening to the Loading Room is to your left.",al={"workshop entrance location","where is the backdoor","gnomeregan backdoor loc"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is this area called the backdoor?",a="The name comes from its use as another way into Gnomeregan’s interior. It skips the main front gauntlet and leads toward the Engineering Labs.",al={"why backdoor","gnomeregan back door","back entrance"},it="name"},{q="Where does this doorway lead inside the city?",a="The doorway opens onto a hallway that leads directly to the Engineering Labs, deep inside Gnomeregan.",al={"where does it go","path through backdoor","what is past the entrance"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is the Workshop Entrance?",a="The Workshop Entrance is a service threshold situated on the far side of the outer workshop beyond the Train Depot. Known colloquially as the backdoor into Gnomeregan, this fortified access point allows passage straight into the Engineering Labs, bypassing the upper city's ceremonial gates.",al={"what is workshop entrance","workshop entrance gnomeregan","about workshop entrance"},it="place",add="bbef9a7d"},{q="What happened at the Workshop Entrance?",a="During the fall of Gnomeregan, the city's secondary access tunnels and freight transit lines became battlegrounds as troggs erupted throughout the lower sub-levels. To prevent the infestation and toxic fallout from spilling uncontrolled into the outer mountain corridors, heavy security protocols and locks were sealed across passage doors like this one.",al={"workshop entrance history","what happened here","backdoor history"},it="history",add="6fa860f5"},{q="Why is the Workshop Entrance ruined and abandoned?",a="When High Tinker Mekkatorque ordered the venting of radioactive gas to purge the invading trogg hordes, the plan backfired catastrophically. The lethal fallout blanketed the industrial infrastructure, sickening the surviving defenders and turning many into feral lepers. The entrance now stands derelict, choked with debris, machinery, and roaming horrors.",al={"why is it abandoned","why is workshop entrance ruined","workshop entrance overrun"},it="ruin",add="8f5e07c5"},{q="Is the Workshop Entrance dangerous?",a="It is extremely hazardous. Beyond the radiation clinging to the lower works, rogue defense automatons, deranged leper gnomes, and bloodthirsty troggs prowl the passageways. Stepping through this doorway places you directly near the city's volatile engineering labs where no sane defense force holds ground.",al={"is workshop entrance safe","workshop entrance dangers","how dangerous is the backdoor"},it="danger",add="e5f19575"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, you know every secret doorway into Gnomeregan could aid the effort to reclaim lost workshops and recover prototype machinery from Mekgineer Thermaplugg’s forces.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can take this corridor toward the Engineering Labs. Cutting-edge schematics may draw tinkerers to infiltrate."},kw={"backdoor","engineering labs","gnomeregan","loading room","train depot","workshop entrance"},rel={"zone:gnomeregan","subzone:train-depot","subzone:loading-room","subzone:engineering-labs"},src={"Workshop Entrance"}}
E["zone:gnomeregan"] = {t="dungeon",n="Gnomeregan",z="gnomeregan",s="In Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan lies ruined and quarantined after the gnomes' desperate defense against troggs. Once their underground capital and greatest technological wonder, it now holds irradiated halls, mutated troggs, deranged leper gnomes, and rogue mechanical sentries. Its surviving people live as refugees in nearby Ironforge.",h="In Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan lies ruined and quarantined after the gnomes' desperate defense against troggs.",sec={{t="A Marvel of Iron and Steam",b="Beneath Dun Morogh, Gnomeregan gathered gnomish invention, competitive craft, and politics under one roof. With help from the nearby dwarves of Ironforge, its people built a vast mechanical complex, powered by grinding engines and whirring gears.\n\nIts intricate ventilation network took fifteen technicians working around the clock to keep fresh air moving. At Tinkers' Court, gnomes debated and competed as their capital grew into a marvel of industry. During the Second War, they sent the Alliance of Lordaeron siege engines, flying machines, and armaments.",sp=0},{t="The Trogg Invasion and the Poisoning",b="During the Third War, as the Scourge tore through Lordaeron, dwarven excavations at the ancient titan vault of Uldaman awakened primitive troggs beneath Dun Morogh. The creatures burrowed into Gnomeregan's lower foundations, and High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque led the defense.\n\nAs the city's defenses began to fail, Mekkatorque followed the counsel of his chief advisor, Mekgineer Thermaplugg. He ordered radioactive waste tanks vented into the lower levels to eradicate the invaders. The toxic gas spread beyond control. Nearly eighty percent of the gnomish population died within days.",sp=0},{t="The Mad Mekgineer's Treason",b="Mekgineer Thermaplugg had secretly coveted High Tinker Mekkatorque's office. Rumors say he knew of the trogg invasion before it began and helped set the disaster in motion. No one verified those rumors, though Mekkatorque believes they could be true. Whatever Thermaplugg intended, events escaped his control.\n\nRadiation failed to kill the troggs and drove them into a violent frenzy, while Thermaplugg was trapped in the contaminated lower tiers. Radioactive sickness twisted him into an insane leper gnome. From his throne in Tinkers' Court, he crowned himself techno-overlord of Gnomeregan and commands mindless leper survivors and erratic machinery.",sp=1},{t="A Fragile Victory",b="From Tinkertown in Ironforge, High Tinker Mekkatorque coordinates the effort to reclaim Gnomeregan. He sends Alliance adventurers into its toxic depths to break Thermaplugg's rule. Slaying the Mekgineer at the heart of Tinkers' Court ends his command over the rogue defenses and leper cohorts.\n\nAt last, the gnomes can avenge his monumental betrayal. Yet a permanent reconquest remains elusive. Irradiated sludge, mutated beasts, and troggs still choke the deeper tunnels. Mekkatorque is assembling gyrodrillmatic excavationators and broader military plans to reclaim his people's ancestral home.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Gnomeregan irradiated?",a="Troggs invaded from below, and High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque tried to destroy them by opening Gnomeregan's radioactive waste tanks on Mekgineer Thermaplugg's advice. The plan was meant to flood only the lower sectors, but deadly radiation seeped throughout the city, killing eighty percent of the gnomish population and mutating survivors.",al={"what happened to gnomeregan","why is gnomeregan green","radiation in gnomeregan"},it="ruin"},{q="Where did all the troggs come from?",a="The troggs were ancient creatures roused from deep subterranean slumber by dwarven archaeological excavations at Uldaman, a titan complex. Drawn to the heat and vibrations of Gnomeregan's heavy machinery, they dug extensive tunnels into the city's lower levels and engineering quarters.",al={"why are there troggs in gnomeregan","trogg origin","trogg invasion"},it="threat"},{q="Why didn't the gnomes ask the Alliance for help against the troggs?",a="The trogg invasion struck during the Third War, as the Scourge brought down the Kingdom of Lordaeron. The gnomes fought with their own technology and soldiers. No record explains why High Tinker Mekkatorque never called for outside aid; he turned instead to venting the city's radioactive waste tanks.",al={"why didn't alliance help gnomeregan","did alliance abandon gnomes"},it="history"},{q="What are leper gnomes?",a="Leper gnomes are survivors of Gnomeregan's radioactive venting, left with severe physical and mental corruption from prolonged exposure. Their skin turned sickly pale green, their bodies became blistered and diseased, and their minds decayed into raving, homicidal mania under Mekgineer Thermaplugg's thrall.",al={"why are the gnomes green and crazy","irradiated gnomes","leper gnome lore"},it="threat"},{q="Who is Mekgineer Thermaplugg?",a="Mekgineer Thermaplugg was High Tinker Mekkatorque's trusted chief advisor, though he secretly coveted the High Tinker office. At his urging, the city was flooded with radiation, and Mekkatorque calls him the betrayer of the gnomish people. Irradiated along with the city, Thermaplugg rules as a deranged leper despot from Tinkers' Court.",al={"thermaplugg","who is the final boss","mekgineer thermaplugg"},it="identity"},{q="What changes after Mekgineer Thermaplugg is defeated?",a="Defeating Thermaplugg cuts off the leadership directing the leper gnomes and rogue defenses. Lethal radiation and thick trogg infestations still choke the lower corridors, so Mekkatorque must prepare deeper excavations before the city can be fully reclaimed.",al={"do we retake gnomeregan","what happens when thermaplugg dies","is gnomeregan saved"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why are the Dark Iron dwarves inside Gnomeregan?",a="The Dark Iron clan sent emissaries into Gnomeregan, represented by the Dark Iron Ambassador. Eager to sabotage Ironforge and the Alliance, the Dark Irons seek an alliance with Thermaplugg and hope to use gnomish technology and weaponized machinery in their own war efforts.",al={"dark iron ambassador","why are dark irons in gnomeregan","dwarves in gnomeregan"},it="allies"},{q="Where are the surviving gnomes living now?",a="After the radioactive catastrophe, the surviving untainted gnomes fled through the mountains to Ironforge. Their dwarven cousins gave them sanctuary in Tinkertown, an engineering enclave within the mountain fortress. There Gelbin Mekkatorque governs his exiled people and plans their eventual homecoming.",al={"where are gnomes living","gnome home city","refugees in ironforge"},it="residents"},{q="What is Gnomeregan?",a="Gnomeregan is the ancient subterranean capital of the gnomes, carved deep into the snowy hills of western Dun Morogh. Built with the aid of the Ironforge dwarves centuries ago, it stood as a monumental triumph of engineering, machinery, and innovation. Today, however, its gleaming metal halls lie poisoned, overrun by mutated troggs and twisted leper gnomes after a catastrophic disaster.",al={"what is gnomeregan","gnomeregan lore","about gnomeregan"},it="place",add="072b7788",nx={10,11}},{q="Was Gnomeregan the capital of the gnomes?",a="Yes. Gnomeregan served as the heart of gnomish society and government for generations. It was the center of gnomish ingenuity, housing their academies, workshops, and the Tinkers' Court where their elected High Tinker ruled. All major inventions and scientific endeavors of the gnome race originated from within these subterranean halls.",al={"was this the gnome capital","is gnomeregan the capital","gnome capital city"},it="history",add="18622943"},{q="Do the gnomes still live in Gnomeregan?",a="Gnomeregan no longer houses the gnomish nation. Eighty percent of the population died when toxic radiation flooded the city, and many who were left behind mutated into insane leper gnomes. Most uncorrupted survivors fled to Tinkertown in Ironforge, though a few engineers and reclamation workers remain in the ruins.",al={"do gnomes live here","are gnomes still in gnomeregan","who lives in gnomeregan now"},it="residents",add="c31b3f81"},{q="Who set off the radiation in Gnomeregan?",a="High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque ordered the emergency venting of the city's radioactive tanks on the advice of his chief advisor, Mekgineer Thermaplugg. The plan was meant to flood only the lower levels to eradicate the trogg invaders, but the radiation killed nearly eighty percent of the gnomes. Thermaplugg, who had secretly coveted the office of High Tinker, is now branded a traitor; rumors that he knew of the trogg invasion beforehand were never verified.",al={"who irradiated gnomeregan","who released the gas","who set off the radiation"},sp=1,it="history",add="46a0252f",nx={13}},{q="Could the gnomes have saved Gnomeregan?",a="No one can say for certain. The trogg invasion struck while the Third War raged, and the gnomes fought it on their own until the desperate venting of the city's radioactive tanks sealed Gnomeregan's fate.",al={"could they have saved the city","could gnomeregan be saved","did gnomeregan have to fall"},it="history",add="bfca8253"},{q="Did the gnomes dig up the troggs?",a="No. The troggs were awakened deep beneath the earth when dwarven explorers excavated the titan vault of Uldaman. Once stirred from their slumber, the troggs tunneled through the mountains toward Ironforge, but were lured away by the loud vibrations and grinding machinery of Gnomeregan.",al={"did gnomes dig up troggs","how were troggs awakened","did gnomes cause troggs"},it="threat",add="6e97b706"},{q="Who is in charge of the gnomes now?",a="High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque remains the elected leader of the gnomes. Despite the tragedy of Gnomeregan, his people hold him in high regard, recognizing his genius and devotion. He currently leads the exiled gnomes from Tinker Town in Ironforge, focused entirely on reclaiming their homeland.",al={"who leads the gnomes","gnome leader","high tinker of the gnomes"},it="in_charge",add="1dd76133",nx={16}},{q="Is there still a gnome king?",a="The gnomes do not have a traditional monarchy; they are a meritocracy led by an elected High Tinker. While Mekkatorque occasionally jokes about calling himself 'King of Gnomes,' the only one claiming the title of royalty inside Gnomeregan is the mad traitor Mekgineer Thermaplugg, who crowned himself techno-overlord.",al={"is there a gnome king","do gnomes have a king","gnome royalty"},it="leader",add="21748788"},{q="Why does the Alliance want me to go into Gnomeregan?",a="High Tinker Mekkatorque and the Alliance need brave adventurers to strike at the heart of the ruined city. They need you to thin the trogg infestation, recover lost technological schematics and data, disrupt Thermaplugg's automated defenses, and ultimately execute the traitor Thermaplugg himself.",al={"why send me into gnomeregan","gnomeregan alliance quest why","why go to gnomeregan"},it="purpose",add="955293ce",nx={18}},{q="What do the gnomes hope to get out of retaking Gnomeregan?",a="Beyond securing justice against Thermaplugg, the gnomes desperately need to recover vital blueprints, power sources, and machinery left behind. Long-term, reclaiming their city would allow gnomanity to end their exile in Ironforge, rebuild their advanced civilization, and restore their standing as an industrial powerhouse for the Alliance.",al={"what do gnomes want from gnomeregan","gnome goals gnomeregan","why retake gnomeregan"},it="motive",add="1f8ae1d4"},{q="Can the leper gnomes be cured?",a="Gnomish scientists like Ozzie Togglevolt and Razzle Sprysprocket are actively studying the toxic residue in hopes of inventing a recombobulation cure. For now, however, the affliction remains irreversible, and most leper gnomes continue to devolve mentally and physically in the toxic fumes.",al={"can leper gnomes be cured","is there a cure for leper gnomes","curing leper gnomes"},it="threat",add="cb78eee3"},{q="Were leper gnomes normal gnomes before?",a="Yes. They were ordinary citizens, inventors, and workers trapped inside the subterranean tunnels during the emergency venting. The toxic radioactive gas warped their bodies, turned their skin sickly green, and ravaged their sanity, leaving them rabid and loyal only to Thermaplugg.",al={"were leper gnomes normal","how leper gnomes made","origin of leper gnomes"},it="threat",add="84ebb566",nx={21}},{q="Do leper gnomes know what they're doing?",a="No. The radiation drove them completely mad. In their delirium, leper gnomes often hallucinate that any outsiders entering the city—even fellow Alliance races—are trogg invaders. Over time, prolonged exposure degrades their minds even further into slobbering wretches.",al={"do leper gnomes have minds","are leper gnomes insane","do leper gnomes think"},it="threat",add="c40f7a95"},{q="What are all these gnome machines fighting me?",a="The mechanical constructs, punch-card sentries, and crowd pummelers you encounter were originally civic defense and utility automata designed to protect the city and maintain order. Mekgineer Thermaplugg seized their master control systems and reprogrammed them to attack any intruders entering his domain.",al={"gnome machines attacking","why are robots hostile in gnomeregan","who controls gnomeregan machines"},it="threat",add="0653d7e6"},{q="Why do the gnomes need outside adventurers instead of their own army?",a="Nearly eighty percent of the gnomish population was wiped out in the catastrophe, leaving their military decimated. The few surviving gnomish soldiers are stretched thin maintaining security and engineering war machines for the Alliance in Ironforge, forcing Mekkatorque to enlist hardened mercenaries and heroes to clear out the toxic ruins.",al={"why need outside adventurers","why not use gnome army","why ask me for gnomeregan"},it="why_me",add="322b05cb"},{q="How did I end up in Gnomeregan?",a="You arrived in Gnomeregan by traveling through the snow-capped foothills of Dun Morogh, heading west past Brewnall Village to the city's massive mechanical entrance gates and descending via its service lifts. Alternatively, Horde adventurers can take a direct teleportation beacon installed in Booty Bay by goblin engineers who take an active, lucrative interest in whatever technology can be salvaged from the ruins.",al={"how did i get here","how do you get into gnomeregan","gnomeregan entrance"},it="arrival",add="300e368c"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Gnomeregan?",a="You are here to strike a blow against the mad traitor Mekgineer Thermaplugg, who seized control of the city after deceiving High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque into bathing its lower levels in toxic radiation. Operating on behalf of the exiled gnomes living in Ironforge—or pursuing salvage and technological secrets—you must push through hordes of irradiated troggs, haywire defense automatons, and crazed leper gnomes to reach the Tinkers' Court and put an end to Thermaplugg's reign.",al={"why am i here","what is my mission here","what to do in gnomeregan"},it="purpose",add="8cb52331"}},ang={["race:Gnome"]="As a gnome, Gnomeregan holds your people's deepest tragedy and enduring shame. Entering its halls is a harrowing pilgrimage to avenge eighty percent of your fallen race and dethrone the traitor Thermaplugg.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, your kinship with the gnomes reaches back to the ancestors who helped lay Gnomeregan's foundations. Dwarven excavations at Uldaman also unwittingly unleashed the trogg hordes that ruined it.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you stand with a people who fought beside the Alliance in the Second War. Liberating Gnomeregan from Thermaplugg is vital to restoring gnomish strength within the faction.",["profession:Engineering"]="As an engineer, you can find advanced masterworks, schematics, and experimental contraptions in Gnomeregan's ruins. Its blueprints remain invaluable amid lethal mechanical chaos."},kw={"dun morogh","gnomeregan","grubbis","leper gnome","mekkatorque","radiation","thermaplugg","tinkers court","trogg","viscous fallout"},rel={"npc:gelbin-mekkatorque","npc:sicco-thermaplugg","zone:dunmorogh","zone:ironforge","topic:gnome","topic:trogg","topic:leper-gnome","subzone:tinkers-court"},m={levels="29-38"},src={"Gnomeregan"}}
